hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3001","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: And I heard Qatadah narrate from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three qualities, whoever has them finds the taste of faith: one who loves a person and loves him only for Allah; one to whom Allah and His Messenger are more beloved than anything else; and one to whom being thrown into the Fire is more beloved than returning to disbelief after Allah saved him from it."
"3002","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of it, except that he said: he finds through them the sweetness of faith."
"3003","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrate from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the Ansar and said: Is there anyone among you from other than you? They said: No, except a nephew of ours. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The nephew of a people is one of them. Then he said: Quraysh are recent in jahiliyyah and calamity, so I wanted to console them and win them over. Are you not pleased that people return with worldly gains while you return with the Messenger of Allah to your homes? If people took a valley and the Ansar took a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar."
"3004","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, life is the life of the Hereafter, so honor the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"3005","Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought meat, and it was said to him: It was given in charity to Barirah. He said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"3006","Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), behind Abu Bakr, behind Umar and Uthman; they would not begin the recitation with In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Shubah said: I said to Qatadah: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Yes, and we asked him about it."
"3007","Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved pumpkin. He said: Food was brought, or he was invited to it. Anas said: I kept following it and placing it before him, for I knew that he loved it."
"3008","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that two men left the presence of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a dark night, with something like two lamps lighting the way before them. He said: When they parted, each one of them had one with him until he reached his family."
"3009","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: I was serving Abu Talhah, Abu Dujanah, and Suhayl ibn Bayda from a waterskin of theirs containing a mixture of unripe and ripe dates, when someone came in to us and said: Something has happened today. We said: What is it? He said: Wine has been forbidden. So we poured it out, and on that day we considered it wine."
"3010","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write to the non-Arabs, and it was said to him: The non-Arabs do not accept a letter except with a seal. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a ring made of silver, and it is as if I am looking at its whiteness on his hand."
"3011","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam grows old while two things stay young in him: greed for wealth and length of life."
"3012","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found a date and said: Were it not that it might be charity, I would have eaten it."
"3013","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The most beloved garment to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the hibarah."
"3014","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people will surely be struck by blackening from the Fire as punishment for sins they committed, then Allah will surely admit them to Paradise by His grace and mercy."
"3015","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Yunus, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate on a table nor in a small bowl, and no refined bread was ever baked for him. He said: I said to Anas: What did they eat on? He said: On travel mats. Abu Musa said: This Yunus is Yunus ibn Abi al-Furat al-Iskaf."
"3016","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged for wine with palm stalks and sandals; then Abu Bakr flogged forty; and when it was Umar's time and people had drawn near from the countryside and villages, he said: What do you think about flogging for wine? Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: I think you should make it like the lightest of the prescribed punishments. He said: So Umar flogged eighty."
"3017","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal has kaf-ra written between his eyes. He said: And Qatadah mentioned that every believer reads it, literate and illiterate; he emerges amid few people and shortage of food; he enters all the cities of the Arabs except Taybah, which is Madinah. Someone said: O Prophet of Allah, does he not want Madinah? He said: Yes indeed, but the angels are lined up at its passes and gates guarding it."
"3018","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Prophet who did not warn his ummah about the one-eyed Dajjal; he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed; written between his eyes is disbeliever."
"3019","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, miserliness, old age, the punishment of the grave, and the trials of life and death."
"3020","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: No one among the people of Paradise wishes to return to this world except the martyr, for he loves to return to this world, saying: that I be killed ten times in the path of Allah, because of what he sees of the honor Allah has given him."
"3021","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) something similar."
"3022","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will be said to the disbeliever: If you had the earth full of gold, would you ransom yourself with it? He will say: Yes. Then it will be said to him: You were asked for something easier than that."
"3023","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet has a supplication with which he supplicated for his ummah, and I have kept my supplication hidden as intercession for my ummah on the Day of Resurrection."
"3024","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas: that a man from the desert people asked the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they were more apt to ask him than his Companions; he said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have prepared nothing for it except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You will be with whom you love. Anas said: I never saw the Muslims rejoice over anything after Islam more than their joy at his saying."
"3025","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas say: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: When is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You are with whom you love."
"3026","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together."
"3027","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no bad omen, and a good omen pleases me. He said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is a good omen? He said: A good word."
"3028","Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrate from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of it, except that he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what is the omen? He said: The good word."
"3029","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, and Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month; Shubah said: cursing, and Hisham said: supplicating against tribes among the Arab tribes, then he left it after bowing; and this last is the saying of Hisham."
"3030","And Shubah said, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, cursing Ril, Dhakwan, and Banu Lihyan."
"3031","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intend to fast; do you have anything? He said: So I brought him a tray with dates and a vessel with water after Bilal had called the adhan. He said: Look for a person to eat. So I went out and found Zayd ibn Thabit, and I invited him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I drank a drink of sawiq and I intend to fast. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I intend to fast. So he ate suhur with him, then prayed two rakahs, then went out and the prayer was established."
"3032","Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, Humayd al-Tawil, and Aban, all from Anas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman begin the recitation with All praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"3033","Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar. And Mamar said, from a son of Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm, he said: My father used to say: None of the people of the supplication remain except me."
"3034","Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah and Aban, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ubayy ibn Kab: My Lord commanded me to recite to you. He said: And did He name me to you? He said: And He named you to me. He said: Then Ubayy wept. Mamar said: Aban said: Anas said: And was I mentioned there?"
"3035","Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: When the bier of Sad ibn Muadh was carried, the hypocrites said: How light his bier is, and that was because of his judgment concerning Banu Qurayzah. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The angels were carrying him."
"3036","Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you we see in ourselves what we love, and when we return to our families and mix with them we disapprove of ourselves. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you remained as you are with me in private, the angels would shake hands with you until they shaded you with their wings openly; but an hour and an hour."
"3037","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit and Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked for water for ablution and did not find any. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Here. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) place his hand in the vessel containing water. He said: Perform ablution in the name of Allah. He said: I saw the water gushing from between his fingers, and the people performed ablution until the last of them had done so. Thabit said: I said to Anas: How many do you think they were? He said: About seventy men."
"3038","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah and Thabit, from Anas, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people will come out of the Fire after the Fire has struck them with blackening, as punishment for sins they did, and Allah will surely bring them out by His grace and mercy and admit them to Paradise."
"3039","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it."
"3040","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are: Maryam daughter of Imran, Khadijah daughter of Khuwaylid, Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, and Asiyah wife of Pharaoh."
"3041","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, he said: Anas said to us: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith which no one will narrate to you after me? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among the signs of the Hour are: knowledge will depart, ignorance will appear, wine will be drunk, adultery will spread, men will decrease and women will increase, until there is one man to look after fifty women."
"3042","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram on the top of the foot because of a pain he had."
"3043","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Thabit, Qatadah, and Aban, all from Anas, he said: When wine was forbidden, he said: On that day I was serving eleven men. He said: They ordered me and I poured it out, and the people poured out their vessels with what was in them until the streets were almost blocked by its smell. Anas said: Their wine on that day was only unripe and ripe dates mixed together. He said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I had an orphan's wealth with me, and I bought wine with it; will you permit me to sell it and return the orphan's wealth to him? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah fight the Jews; animal fats were forbidden to them, yet they sold them and ate their prices. And he did not permit him to sell wine."
"3044","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, concerning His saying: Evil was the morning of those warned: when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Khaybar, he found them as they went out to their crops carrying their spades; when they saw him with the army, they turned back and returned to their fortress. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greatest, Khaybar is ruined; when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned."
"3045","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: A group from Ukl and Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - thus Mamar said - he said: They spoke of Islam, and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that they were people of livestock, not people of countryside produce, and Madinah did not suit them, and they complained of its unhealthiness to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered some camels for them and appointed a herdsman for them, and said: Go out of Madinah and drink from their urine and milk. They went and settled near al-Harrah, disbelieved after their Islam, killed the herdsman, and drove off the camels. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent after them, and they were brought; he cut off their hands and feet, branded their eyes, and they were left near al-Harrah biting its stones until they died. Qatadah said: We were told that this verse was revealed concerning them: The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and strive to spread corruption in the land, to the end of the verse."
"3046","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: There was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That Allah may forgive you your past and future sins, upon his return from al-Hudaybiyah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A verse has been revealed to me that is more beloved to me than what is on the earth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it. They said: Congratulations, O Prophet of Allah; Allah has made clear what He will do with you, so what will He do with us? Then was revealed: That He may admit the believing men and believing women, until it reached: a great triumph."
"3047","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man said: O Prophet of Allah, how will the disbeliever be gathered on his face on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Is not the One Who made him walk on his feet in this world able to make him walk on his face on the Day of Resurrection? Qatadah said: Yes indeed, by the might of our Lord."
"3048","Zuhayr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah say: I asked Anas ibn Malik: How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: He used to prolong it with prolongation."
"3049","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on the two jugular veins and the upper back."
"3050","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None believes until I am more beloved to him than his father, his child, and all people."
"3051","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Safiyyah daughter of Huyayy, and made her freedom her dowry."
"3052","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Dajjal will come to Madinah and find the angels guarding it, so neither the Dajjal nor the plague will enter it, if Allah wills."
"3053","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting. They said: O Messenger of Allah, but you fast continuously. He said: You are not like me; I spend the night being fed and given drink."
"3054","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after having drunk wine, so he ordered and he was struck with two sandals forty times. Then a man who had drunk wine was brought to Abu Bakr, and he did the same with him. Then a man who had drunk wine was brought to Umar, and he consulted the people about that. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: I think you should make it the least of the prescribed punishments, eighty. So Umar struck him eighty."
"3055","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdillah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people will surely be struck by blackening from the Fire as punishment for sins they did, then Allah will admit them to Paradise by His grace and mercy; they will be called the Jahannamis."
"3056","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is the completion, or part of the completion, of the prayer."
"3057","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one enters Paradise who wishes to leave it, even if he has all that is on the earth, except the martyr, for he wishes to return and be killed ten times because of what he sees of honor."
"3058","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month after bowing."
"3059","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: There was a tree in the people's path that harmed people, so a man came and removed it from the people's path. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw him rolling about in its shade in Paradise."
"3060","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was once invited to barley bread and rancid melted fat."
"3061","He said: And I heard him one day saying: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is not with Muhammad a sa of grain nor a sa of dates, though on that day he had nine wives."
"3062","He said: And he mortgaged a coat of mail of his with a Jew in Madinah, taking food from him, and he could not find the means to redeem it."
"3063","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith which no one after me will narrate having heard it from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among the signs of the Hour are: knowledge will be taken away, ignorance will appear, wine will be drunk, adultery will spread, men will decrease and women will increase, until there is one caretaker for fifty women."
"3064","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third valley; nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust; and Allah turns to whoever turns."
"3065","Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection and will be concerned about that. He said: They will say: If only we sought intercession to our Lord so He would relieve us from this place of ours. He said: They will go until they come to Adam, and say: O Adam, you are the father of mankind; Allah created you with His Hand, made His angels prostrate to you, and taught you the names of all things; intercede for us with your Lord so He would relieve us from this place of ours. He said: Then he will say: I am not the one for that, and he will mention his sin of eating from the tree. He said: He will say: But go to Nuh, the first messenger Allah sent. He said: They will go until they come to Nuh, and he will say: I am not the one for that, and he will mention his sin of asking his Lord for what he had no knowledge of. He said: He will say: Go to Ibrahim, the close friend of the Most Merciful. He said: They will go until they come to Ibrahim, and he will say: I am not the one for that, and he will mention his three lies: his saying: Rather the eldest of them did it, and his saying: I am sick, and his saying when he came upon the tyrant: Tell him I am your brother, for I will tell him you are my sister, for we are two brothers in the Book of Allah, there are no two believers on earth besides us. He said: He will say: But go to Musa, to whom Allah spoke and gave the Torah. They will go until they come to Musa, and he will say: I am not the one for that, and he will mention his sin he committed before. He said: He will say: But go to Isa, servant of Allah and His Messenger, and Allah's word and spirit. He said: They will go until they come to Isa, and he will say: I am not the one for that, but go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whose past and future sins Allah has forgiven. He said: Then they will come to me, and I will seek permission from my Lord and permission will be given to me. When I see Him I will fall prostrate, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then He will say to me: Raise your head, O Muhammad; speak and you will be heard; intercede and you will be granted intercession; ask and you will be given. So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praises He will teach me. Then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them to Paradise. Then I will return to my Lord a second time; when I see my Lord I will fall prostrate, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then it will be said to me: Raise your head, Muhammad; speak and you will be heard; intercede and you will be granted intercession; ask and you will be given. So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praise He will teach me. Then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them to Paradise. Then I will return a third time to my Lord; when I see my Lord I will fall prostrate, and He will leave me as long as Allah wills to leave me. Then it will be said to me: Raise your head, Muhammad; speak and you will be heard; intercede and you will be granted intercession; ask and you will be given. So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with praise He will teach me. Then I will intercede, and a limit will be set for me, and I will bring them out of the Fire and admit them to Paradise, until I return to my Lord, and it will be said a fourth time. He said: Then I will say: O Lord, none remain in the Fire except those held back by the Quran. He said: He will say: Eternal stay has become obligatory upon him. Qatadah said: Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a praised station: he said: This is the praised station which Allah, Blessed and Exalted, promised His Prophet, peace be upon him."
"3066","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Hajjaj al-Ahwal al-Bahili narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who sleeps through prayer or is heedless of it. He said: Its expiation is to pray it when he remembers it."
"3067","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands in any of his supplication, or at any of his supplication, except in the prayer for rain, for he would raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen."
"3068","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands in any supplication except in the prayer for rain, for he would raise them until his armpits showed."
"3069","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer while completing it."
"3070","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month after bowing, supplicating against tribes among the Arab tribes."
"3071","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which no one after me will narrate to you, having heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among the signs of the Hour are: knowledge will be taken away, ignorance will appear, wine will be drunk, adultery will spread, men will decrease and women will increase, until there is one caretaker for fifty women."
"3072","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Khosrow, Caesar, and Ukaydir of Dumah, calling them to Allah."
"3073","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man from the desert people asked the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they were more apt to ask him than his Companions, and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have prepared nothing much for it, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You will be with whom you love. Anas said: I never saw the people rejoice over anything after Islam more than their joy at his saying."
"3074","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kaf-ra is written between his eyes. Abu Said said: meaning disbeliever. Qatadah said: And we were told that every believer reads it, literate and illiterate; and he emerges amid few people and shortage of food; and he enters all the cities of the Arabs except Taybah, which is Madinah. Someone said: O Prophet of Allah, does he not want Madinah? He said: Yes indeed, but the angels are lined up at its passes guarding it."
"3075","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muadh narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, miserliness, cowardice, old age, the punishment of the grave, and the trials of life and death."
"3076","Ubaydullah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, that when the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write to the non-Arabs, it was said to him: The non-Arabs do not accept a letter except with a seal on it. So he had a ring made of silver, and it is as if I am looking at its whiteness on his hand."
"3077","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two white rams, naming Allah and saying takbir. He said: I saw him slaughter them with his own hand, placing his foot on their sides."
"3078","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ubaydillah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Mamar, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to put on sandals while standing."
"3079","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Saminah al-Shami narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the house of Aishah and saw meat, and said: Roast some of it for us. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is charity. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Roast some of it for us, for it has reached its proper place."
"3080","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Umar al-Abdi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not from abundance of goods, but richness is richness of the soul."
"3081","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Fahd ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is like the ear of grain, bending sometimes and standing straight sometimes."
"3082","Ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A servant does not attain the reality of faith until he loves for people what he loves for himself of good."
"3083","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai and Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month after bowing only."
"3084","Zuhayr narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, that Umm Sulaym menstruated after having performed tawaf al-ifadah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to depart."
"3085","Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Abbad narrated to us, the like of it."
"3086","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith which no one after me will narrate to you, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Among the signs of the Hour are: knowledge will be taken away, ignorance will descend, wine will be drunk, women will increase and men will decrease, until there is one caretaker for fifty women."
"3087","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sleeps through a prayer or forgets it, let him pray it when he remembers it."
"3088","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."
"3089","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin and its expiation is burying it."
"3090","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who narrated to them, that a Jewish man passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Death be upon you. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answered him back. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He only said: Death be upon you. So he called him and he admitted it. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Answer him back as he said."
"3091","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, that it was said to Anas: Which clothing was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The hibarah."
"3092","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, he said: I asked Anas: How many Hajj did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform? He said: One Hajj, and he performed four Umrahs: his Umrah from al-Hudaybiyah, his Umrah from al-Jiranah in Dhu al-Qadah when he distributed the spoils of Hunayn, and his Umrah with his Hajj."
"3093","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Prophet was sent but that he warned his ummah about the one-eyed liar; indeed he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed; written between his eyes is: disbeliever."
"3094","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, Thabit, and Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to begin the prayer with All praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; and Humayd would not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3095","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pass by a date, and nothing would prevent him from taking it except fear that it was charity."
"3096","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Simak narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Bara'ah with Abu Bakr to the people of Makkah, then called him back and sent Ali, and said: None conveys it except a man from my household."
"3097","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month, then left it."
"3098","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet has a supplication with which he supplicated and it was answered for him; and I have kept my supplication hidden as intercession for my ummah on the Day of Resurrection."
"3099","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would let his hair reach his shoulders."
"3100","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting. He said: It was said to him: You fast continuously. He said: I spend the night, my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."
"3101","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that a man entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in prayer, and said: Praise be to Allah, pure and blessed. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: Which of you said such-and-such words? The people fell silent three times. He said: A man from the people said: I said them, and I intended nothing but good by them. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Twelve angels raced to take them, and they did not know how to write them until they asked their Lord. He said: Write them as My servant said."
"3102","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sandals with two straps."
"3103","And with its chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade steeping unripe dates and ripe dates together."
"3104","He said: Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, the like of it."
"3105","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on the pulpit, and said: O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah for rain for us. So he prayed for rain, and we saw no patch of cloud in the sky, then it rained on us and it did not stop except that its two rocky tracts rained. The following Friday, that man or another stood up to him and said: Ask Allah to lift it. He said: I kept looking at the clouds splitting to the right and left around Madinah, while not a drop rained inside it."
"3106","Zuhayr narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"3107","Zuhayr narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel, and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Woe to you, ride it."
"3108","Zuhayr narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you spits, let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his left foot."
"3109","Zuhayr narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never had bread and meat together for lunch and dinner except when food was scarce and shared."
"3110","Zuhayr narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, its expiation is only to pray it when he remembers it."
"3111","Zuhayr narrated to us: Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ibn Umm Maktum in charge of Madinah twice. He said: And I saw him on the day of al-Qadisiyyah carrying a black banner."
"3112","Zuhayr narrated to us: Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us: al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us: from Matar: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking while standing, and eating while standing."
"3113","Zuhayr narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that a cloak of sundus (fine silk) was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), though he used to forbid silk. The people admired it, so he said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, the handkerchiefs of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in Paradise are better than this."
"3114","Zuhayr narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the people of Makkah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to show them a sign, so he showed them the splitting of the moon twice."
"3115","Zuhayr narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that a Jew came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: As-sam upon you (death upon you). The people returned the greeting, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what he said? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best; he greeted you, O Prophet of Allah. He said: No, but he said such-and-such; bring him back to me. So they brought him back, and he said: Did you say as-sam upon you? He said: Yes. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of the People of the Book greets you, say: And upon you. He said: Upon you what you said. {And when they come to you, they greet you with what Allah has not greeted you with}."
"3116","al-Abbas ibn al-Walid an-Narsi narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will be seen in it silver jugs as many as the stars of the sky and more, meaning the Hawd (the Pool)."
"3117","al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Yazid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: that Anas narrated to them: that Umm Sulaym narrated that she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: If a woman sees that, let her take a bath. Umm Sulaym said: And I felt shy about that, and I said: Can that happen? So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes; how else would resemblance come about? The fluid of the man is thick, and the fluid of the woman is thin and yellow; from whichever of them dominates or precedes, the resemblance comes."
"3118","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ad-Dawraqi narrated to us: Mubashshir narrated to us: from al-Awza'i: from Qatadah: from Anas and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in my ummah division and a faction who speak good words but do evil deeds; they will recite the Quran and it will not pass their throats; they will pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the prey, then they will not return to it until it returns to its bowstring. They are the worst of creation. Glad tidings to whoever kills them, and glad tidings to whoever they kill. They call to the Book of Allah but have nothing to do with it. Whoever fights them is more deserving before Allah than them. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their mark? He said: Shaving the head."
"3119","al-Hakam ibn Musa Abu Salih narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: from al-Hajjaj: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned black-and-white rams. He brought one of them near and said: In the name of Allah; O Allah, from You and to You; this is on behalf of Muhammad and his household. And he brought the other near and said: In the name of Allah; O Allah, from You and to You; this is on behalf of whoever affirms Your oneness from my ummah."
"3120","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isa at-Tabba' narrated to us: from Abbad ibn al-Awwam: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear his ring on his right hand."
"3121","Ammar Abu Yasir al-Mustamli narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Ibrahim Abu Hatim al-Hajari narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: from Anas, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a flea bit a man and he cursed it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not curse it, for it woke up a prophet among the prophets for prayer."
"3122","Ammar also narrated to us: Yusuf narrated to us: Qatadah and Abdullah ad-Danaj and Matar al-Warraq all narrated to us: from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out from the door of the house intending the chamber, and he heard people disputing about divine decree, saying: Did Allah not say such-and-such verse? Did Allah not say such-and-such verse? He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opened the door of the chamber, and it was as if pomegranate seeds had burst open on his face, and he said: Were you commanded with this, or were you meant for this? Those before you perished only because of things like this: they struck parts of the Book of Allah against others. Allah commanded you with a matter, so follow it, and forbade you, so refrain. He said: So after that the people never heard anyone speaking (about it) until Ma'bad al-Juhani came, and al-Hajjaj seized him and killed him."
"3123","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: {O mankind, fear your Lord} up to His saying {but the punishment of Allah is severe} was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on a journey of his. He raised his voice with it until his companions gathered to him, and he said: Do you know which day? This is the day Allah will say to Adam: Rise and send forth a contingent to the Fire: from every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise. That weighed heavily upon the Muslims, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be steadfast, draw near, and rejoice; for by the One in whose Hand is my soul, you among mankind are but like a mole on the side of a camel, or like a mark on the foreleg of a beast. With you are two created multitudes that were never in anything but they multiplied it: Gog and Magog, and those who perished among the disbelievers of the jinn and mankind."
"3124","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us: from Qatadah: from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, concerning His saying {He frowned and turned away}: Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was speaking to Ubayy ibn Khalaf, so he turned away from him, and Allah revealed {He frowned and turned away}. He said: After that the Prophet used to honor him. Qatadah said: And Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said: I saw him on the day of al-Qadisiyyah wearing armor and carrying a black banner, meaning Ibn Umm Maktum."
"3125","Musa ibn Abdur-Rahman as-Sulami narrated to us: Umar ibn Sa'id al-Abahh narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a virgin in her private chamber, and when he disliked something it was recognized on his face."
"3126","Musa ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to us: Umar ibn Sa'id narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed through a road of the roads of Madinah, the scent of musk was found from him. They would say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed through this road today."
"3127","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us: my father narrated to me: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon Anjashah while he was driving his womenfolk (camels), and said: O Anjashah, gently; do not break the glass vessels."
"3128","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: from Hisham: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck for wine-drinking with sandals and palm stalks, and Abu Bakr lashed with his hand. When Umar's time came and people drew near from the villages and the countryside, he mentioned that to his companions, so Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf said: Make it like the lightest of the prescribed punishments. So he lashed eighty."
"3129","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: from Hisham: Qatadah narrated to us: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman used to begin the recitation with {All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds}."
"3130","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: from Sufyan: from Ma'mar: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went around his wives with a single washing."
"3131","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' and Khalid ibn al-Harith both narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"3132","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: that Anas informed them that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman used to begin the recitation in their prayers with {All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds}."
"3133","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and married her, and made her freeing her dowry."
"3134","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met the enemy, he would say: O Allah, You are my strength and my helper, and by You I fight."
"3135","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us, if Allah wills, thus he said: from Qatadah: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The people asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they pressed him with questions, so he said: You will not ask me about anything but I will explain it. Then a man stood up who, when he quarreled, was attributed to other than his father, and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab stood up and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, and with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger; we seek refuge in Allah from the evil of trials. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have never seen the like of today in good and evil; Paradise and Hellfire were depicted to me."
"3136","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Abu Amir narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a similar narration, but in the hadith of Hisham he did not say: If Allah wills."
"3137","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two black-and-white horned rams, slaughtering them with his hand, as if I am looking at their sides with his foot upon them, pronouncing the name of Allah and remembering Allah."
"3138","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' and Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the completion of prayer."
"3139","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Abdur-Rahman narrated to us: from Imran al-Qattan: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ibn Umm Maktum in charge of Madinah twice. He said: I saw him on the day of al-Qadisiyyah carrying a black banner."
"3140","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Uhud and said: Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it."
"3141","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be cast into the Fire and it will say: Is there any more, until the Blessed and Exalted places His leg in it, or he said: His foot, and it will say: Enough, enough."
"3142","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id and Harami both said: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3143","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things, whoever has them finds the sweetness of faith: whoever loves a person and loves him only for Allah; and whoever for whom Allah and His Messenger are dearer to him than anything else; and whoever being thrown into the Fire is dearer to him than returning to disbelief after Allah saved him from it."
"3144","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Harami narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth he would seek a second to it, and if he had a second he would seek a third to it; nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents. He said: So I do not know whether it is something Allah revealed or something he used to say."
"3145","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I enter prayer intending to lengthen it, then I hear the voice of a child and I shorten my prayer, because I know how intense his mother's distress is from that."
"3146","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Harami narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah, he said: I asked Anas about nabidh (fermented drink). He said: I never heard anything about it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3147","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Harami narrated to me: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas ibn Malik: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two, with his two fingers: the index and the middle."
"3148","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Harami narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"3149","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Harami narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf and az-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam to wear silk because of an itch that was in them."
"3150","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdul-Wahid ibn Abi Hazm al-Quta'i narrated to us: Umar ibn Amir narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that a Jew passed by a young girl wearing jewelry, snatched her jewelry and threw her into a well. She was reached and taken out while still alive, and it was said: Who killed you? She said: So-and-so the Jew. So he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he killed him."
"3151","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"3152","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating: from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, none of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself of good."
"3153","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: from Anas, he said: There was an alarm in Madinah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode a horse belonging to Abu Talhah that was slow and cutting its gait. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and said: We found it to be an ocean among oceans. He said: And it could not be outrun after that."
"3154","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas ibn Malik: that he mentioned: that a Jew passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was with his companions, or he said: and with him were his companions, and greeted him. He said: Do you know what he said? They said: No. He said: Bring him back to me. He said: Did you say: Death upon you? He said: Yes. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the People of the Book greet you, say: And upon you."
"3155","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to write to the non-Arabs, was told: They do not accept a letter except with a seal. He said: So he took a seal and engraved in it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"3156","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that a Jew killed a slave-girl for silver ornaments, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed him."
"3157","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, concerning spitting in the mosque: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."
"3158","Abu Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the bowing and the prostration, for by Allah, I see you from behind my back when you bow and when you prostrate. Then Qatadah said: Allah shows him of that what you do not see."
"3159","Abu Musa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, except that he did not say: Allah shows him."
"3160","Abu Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, and Abdul-A'la: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I enter prayer intending to lengthen it, then I hear the crying of a child, so I shorten my prayer because I know how intense his mother's anguish is from his crying."
"3161","Abu Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached by Ri'l and Dhakwan and Usayyah and Banu Lihyan, claiming they had embraced Islam, and they sought his help against their people. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reinforced them with seventy of the Ansar. Anas said: We used to call them in their time the Reciters; they would strive by day and pray by night. They set out with them until when they reached Bi'r Ma'unah, they betrayed them and killed them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated in the dawn prayer for a month against these tribes: Ri'l and Dhakwan and Usayyah and Banu Lihyan. Qatadah said: And Anas narrated to us that they recited concerning them a Quran: Convey from us to our people that we met our Lord and He was pleased with us and pleased us."
"3162","Abu Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, and Abdul-A'la: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky in their prayer? His speech about that was stern until he said: They will stop doing that, or their sight will be snatched away."
"3163","Abu Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, and Abdul-A'la: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Phlegm in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."
"3164","Abu Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Zayd ibn Thabit took the pre-dawn meal. When he finished his sahur, meaning I said to him: How long was between it and his entering prayer? He said: As much as a man recites fifty verses."
"3165","Abu Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the front row, and if there is any shortfall, let it be in the last row."
"3166","Abu Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, and Abdul-A'la: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that Umm Sulaym asked the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If that happens in her dream, let her take a bath. Umm Sulaym said: And I felt shy about that, so I said: Can that happen? So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes; how else would resemblance come about? The fluid of the man is thick and white, and the fluid of the woman is yellow and thin; whichever of them dominates or precedes, the resemblance comes from it."
"3167","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade a man to drink standing. Qatadah said: So we said: What about eating? He said: That is worse, or more foul."
"3168","Abu Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two black-and-white horned rams, stepping on their sides and slaughtering them with his hand, and saying: In the name of Allah, and Allah is Greatest."
"3169","Abu Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you."
"3170","Abu Musa narrated to us: Abdul-A'la narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer while completing it."
"3171","Abu Musa narrated to us: Abdul-A'la narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in his prayer, let him not spit in front of him nor before him, for he is conversing with his Lord; but to his left, or under his left foot."
"3172","Abu Musa narrated to us: Abdul-A'la narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that a group from Ukl and Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we were people of livestock and were not people of the countryside. He said: So they found Madinah unhealthy, and he ordered for them some milch camels and a herdsman that they go out with them and drink from their urine and milk. Then they killed the herdsman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), drove off the camels, and disbelieved after their Islam. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent in pursuit of them, and they were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet, branded their eyes, and left them in the lava field until they died."
"3173","Abu Musa narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) climbed Uhud, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman followed him, and it trembled beneath them. So he said: Be still: a Prophet, and a truthful one, and two martyrs."
"3174","Abu Musa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far Ghundar narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at az-Zawra, and a vessel containing water that did not cover his fingers, or he said: what would cover his fingers, was brought. He ordered his companions to perform ablution, and placed his palm in the water, and we would see the water gushing from between his fingers until the people performed ablution. We said to Anas: How many were you that day? He said: Three hundred, or about three hundred."
"3175","Abu Musa narrated to us: Abdul-A'la narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah bint Huyayy and made her freeing her dowry."
"3176","Abu Musa narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: from Abu Talhah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prevailed over a people, he liked to stay in their courtyard three days."
"3177","Abu Musa narrated to us: Abdul-Aziz ibn Abdus-Samad narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around his wives in one night."
"3178","Abu Musa narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us: my father narrated to me: from Qatadah: from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around his wives in an hour of the night and day, and they were eleven. He said: I said to Anas ibn Malik: Could he manage that? He said: We used to say he had been given the strength of forty."
"3179","Abu Musa narrated to us: Abdul-A'la narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, its expiation is to pray it when he remembers it."
"3180","Abu Musa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which none will narrate to you after me who heard it from him? It is among the signs of the Hour: that knowledge will be lifted, and ignorance will appear, and adultery will spread, and wine will be drunk, and men will go away and women will remain, until there is for fifty women a single caretaker."
"3181","Abu Musa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating: from Anas: that the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The People of the Book greet us, so how should we return to them? He said: Say: And upon you."
"3182","Abu Musa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating: from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said: When the servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit; and when he draws near a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom; and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"3183","Abu Musa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating: from Anas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and I do not know whether it is something revealed or something he said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth he would wish, or he would seek, a third valley to them; nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"3184","Abu Musa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating: from Anas ibn Malik: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None of you believes until he loves for his brother and for his neighbor what he loves for himself."
"3185","Abu Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us: from Husayn al-Mu'allim: from Qatadah: from Anas: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, no servant believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."
"3186","Muhammad ibn Mahdi Abu Abdullah al-Ubulli narrated to us in Basrah: Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Buraq, saddled and bridled, on the night he was taken by night. It proved difficult for him, so Jibril said to it: Would you do this with Muhammad? None more noble before Allah than him ever rode you. He said: So al-Buraq broke out in sweat."
"3187","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us: from Qatadah, concerning Allah's saying {At the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary}: Anas ibn Malik informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary was raised for me in the seventh heaven; its fruits like the jars of Hajar, and its leaves like the ears of elephants. From its trunk come out two visible rivers and two hidden rivers. I said: O Jibril, what is this? He said: As for the two hidden rivers, they are in Paradise; and as for the two visible, they are the Nile and the Euphrates."
"3188","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us: from Qatadah: from Anas, concerning His saying {Indeed, We have given you al-Kawthar}: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw al-Kawthar, a river in Paradise, its banks domes of pearl. I said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is al-Kawthar which Allah has given you."
"3189","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us: from Qatadah: from Anas: The people of Makkah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a sign, so the moon split in Makkah twice. Then he said: {The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split * And if they see a sign, they turn away and say: Passing magic}, meaning: going away."
"3190","Muhammad narrated to us: Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the completion of prayer is straightening the row."
"3191","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Complete the bowing and the prostration, for by Allah, I see you from behind my back when you bow or prostrate."
"3192","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas ibn Malik: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let none of you spit in his prayer in front of him nor to his right, for he is conversing with his Lord."
"3193","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid and Yahya both said: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the sky in their prayer? His speech about that was stern until he said: They will stop doing that, or their sight will be snatched away."
"3194","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sleeps through prayer or misses it, let him pray it when he remembers it. Allah said: {And establish prayer for My remembrance}."
"3195","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a vessel containing water enough to cover his fingers or not cover them, Sa'id doubted. They began performing ablution, and the water began gushing from between his fingers. He said: So we said to Anas: How many were you? He said: Three hundred. Khalid said: Then he mentioned a word, then he said: Three hundred."
"3196","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel, and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you."
"3197","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking standing. He said: And he was asked about eating standing? Khalid said: I do not know who was asked. He said: That is worse, or he said: That is more foul."
"3198","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid and Yazid ibn Zuray' both said: Sa'id narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) climbed Uhud with Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, and the mountain trembled beneath them. In the hadith of Yazid: So he struck with his foot and said: Be firm, O Uhud, for upon you are only a Prophet and a truthful one and two martyrs."
"3199","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah, he said: Anas ibn Malik said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be seen in it jugs of gold and silver like the number of the stars of the sky. Abu Sa'id said: Meaning his Pool."
"3200","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: that Anas informed them, concerning those who collected the Quran in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that they were Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and Zayd, and Abu Zayd. He said: And all of them were of the Ansar."
"3201","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, or from some people among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that they would lay their sides down and sleep; among them were those who performed ablution, and among them were those who did not perform ablution."
"3202","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Harami narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: My mother said: O Prophet of Allah, your servant; supplicate to Allah for him. He said: O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, and bless for him in what You have given him."
"3203","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Harami narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked pumpkin, and I saw him one day eating food containing pumpkin, and I began bringing it near to him."
"3204","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas: {Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory}: He said: al-Hudaybiyyah."
"3205","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Mu'adh narrated to us: from his father: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around his wives in an hour of the night and day, and they were eleven. So I said to Anas: Could he manage that? He said: We used to say he had been given the strength of thirty."
"3206","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: from Sa'id: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: This verse was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his return from al-Hudaybiyyah; it was revealed while his companions were mingled with grief, and they had been prevented from their rites, so they slaughtered the sacrificial animals at al-Hudaybiyyah. When this verse was revealed, he said to his companions: A verse has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than the whole world. When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it, a man among the people said: Congratulations, O Prophet of Allah; Allah has made clear to us what He will do with you, so what will He do with us? Then Allah revealed after it: {That He may admit the believing men and the believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow}, the verse."
"3207","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us: from Qatadah: that Anas narrated to them that Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf married a woman for the weight of a date-pit of gold."
"3208","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Some people will come out of the Fire after being touched by its scorch, and will enter Paradise; they will be called the Jahannamis (people of Hell)."
"3209","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ad-Dawraqi narrated to us: Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: Anas ibn Malik informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the Ansar and said: Is there among you anyone from other than you? They said: No, except a sister's son of ours. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sister's son of a people is from themselves, or he said: from the people."
"3210","Ahmad narrated to us: Hajjaj narrated to me: Shu'bah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating: from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ansar are my inner garment and my outer garment; people will increase and they will decrease, so accept from their doers of good and pardon their doers of wrong."
"3211","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu an-Nadr narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: There is no life but the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"3212","Ahmad narrated to us: Bahz narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me that he heard Anas ibn Malik narrating: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no bad omen, and the good omen pleases me. He said: So I said: What is the good omen? He said: The good word."
"3213","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Hisham informed us: from Qatadah: Anas heard him saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no bad omen. Then he mentioned a narration like that of Bahz, except that he said: The good omen is the good word."
"3214","Ahmad narrated to us: Bahz narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: from Anas ibn Malik: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the completion of prayer."
"3215","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah, he said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of the completion of prayer. Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah said: I was lenient in this; I did not ask Qatadah whether he heard it or not."
"3216","Ahmad narrated to us: Bahz narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Qatadah informed us: from Anas: They said: O Messenger of Allah, when the People of the Book greet us, how should we return to them? He said: Say: Upon you."
"3217","Ahmad narrated to us: Bahz narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast continuously. They said: But you fast continuously. He said: You are not in that like me; I spend the day, or he said: I spend the night, fed and given drink."
"3218","Ahmad narrated to us: Bahz and Wahb ibn Jarir both said: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be moderate in prostration, and let none of you spread his forearms as the dog spreads them."
"3219","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: Woe to you, or: Woe unto you, ride it."
"3220","Ahmad narrated to us: Shababah narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ride it. Then he mentioned a narration like that of Bahz."
"3221","Ahmad narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: A man who had drunk wine was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered concerning him and he was struck with two sandals forty times. Then a man who had drunk wine was brought to Abu Bakr, and he did the like with him. Then a man who had drunk wine was brought to Umar, and he consulted the people about that. Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf said: The least of the prescribed punishments is eighty. So Umar struck him eighty."
"3222","Ahmad ad-Dawraqi narrated to us: Bahz narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in prayer, he is conversing with his Lord, so let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but let him spit to his left under his left foot."
"3223","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: Anas ibn Malik heard him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in prayer, he is only conversing with his Lord, so let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but to his left under his foot."
"3224","And Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us: from Qatadah: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spittle in the mosque is a sin; its expiation is burying it."
"3225","Bahz narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: from Anas, he said: There was an alarm in Madinah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a horse belonging to Abu Talhah called Mandub. He rode it and said: We saw no alarm. And we found it to be an ocean."
"3226","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Amir al-Qaysi narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No one enters Paradise and is pleased to come out of it, even if he has all that is on earth, except the martyr; he wishes to return and be killed ten times for what he sees of honor."
"3227","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed me, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a suit of silk, and they began touching it and marveling at its softness. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The handkerchiefs of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in Paradise are better than this. Or: softer than this. Shu'bah said: Then Qatadah narrated to me: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of this."
"3228","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none wish for death because of harm that has befallen him; but if he must do so, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me."
"3229","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Mu'adh: Know that whoever dies bearing witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, truthfully from his heart, enters Paradise."
"3230","Ahmad narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Abi at-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: When it was the day of the Conquest and Quraysh came in the morning, the Ansar said: By Allah, this is strange; our swords drip with the blood of Quraysh, yet our spoils are divided among them. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent for the Ansar specifically and said: What is this that has reached me about you? He said: And they would not lie. They said: It is what reached you. He said: Are you not pleased that people go with the spoils and you return with the Messenger of Allah to your homes? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people took a valley, or he said: a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar. Shu'bah said: And Qatadah narrated to us: from Anas ibn Malik with a similar narration, and added in it. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the Ansar specifically and said: Is there among you anyone from other than you? They said: No, except a sister's son of ours. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sister's son of a people is from them. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Quraysh are recently of the time of ignorance, and I wanted to reconcile them and comfort them."
"3231","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: And Hisham narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for a month after bowing against some tribes of the Arabs, then he left it."
"3232","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: Anas heard him narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted said: I am with My servant's thought of Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me."
"3233","Ahmad narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a supplication with which he supplicated for his ummah, and I have kept my supplication hidden as intercession for my ummah on the Day of Resurrection."
"3234","Ahmad narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated it to me: Shu'bah informed us: from Qatadah: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said of Madinah: The Dajjal will come to it and find the angels guarding it, so the Dajjal will not enter it."
"3235","Ahmad narrated to us: Hajjaj narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to me: from Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from Ubadah ibn as-Samit: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him."
"3236","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us: from Qatadah: Anas ibn Malik heard him: from Ubadah: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of Hajjaj."
"3237","Ahmad narrated to us: Shababah narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas ibn Malik: from Ubadah ibn as-Samit: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The dream of the Muslim is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"3238","Ahmad narrated to us: Hajjaj narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: I heard Qatadah: from Anas ibn Malik: from Umm Sulaym: that she said: O Messenger of Allah, Anas is your servant; supplicate to Allah for him. So he said: O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, and bless for him in what You have given him. Anas said: One of my children informed me that more than a hundred of my children and my grandchildren were buried."
"3239","Ahmad narrated to us: Hajjaj narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Hisham ibn Zayd narrating from Anas ibn Malik with the like of that."
"3240","Ahmad narrated to us: Shababah narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sleep, then pray without performing ablution."
"3241","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us: from Qatadah, he said: I asked Anas about the nabidh of jars. He said: I never heard anything about it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Anas used to dislike it."
"3242","Ahmad narrated to us: Shababah narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: There was an alarm in Madinah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed a horse belonging to Abu Talhah called Mandub. He said: So he rode, and when he returned, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We saw no alarm. And we found it to be an ocean."
"3243","Ahmad narrated to us: Bahz narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Qatadah informed us: from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved pumpkin, or gourd. He said: So I saw him one day eating it. He said: So I began placing it before him."
"3244","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us: from Qatadah: Anas ibn Malik heard him: that meat was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: What is this? They said: Something given in charity to Barirah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is charity for her and a gift for us."
"3245","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and behind Abu Bakr, and behind Umar, and behind Uthman, and they would not begin the recitation with (In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate). Shu'bah said: I said to Qatadah: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Yes; I asked Anas about it."
"3246","Ahmad narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah: from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b when {Those who disbelieved} was revealed: Allah has commanded me to recite to you: {Those who disbelieved}. He said: Did He name me to you? He said: Yes. He said: So he wept."
"3247","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Hisham informed us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two black-and-white horned rams, pronouncing the name of Allah and magnifying Him, and I saw him placing his foot upon their sides."
"3248","Ahmad narrated to us: Shababah narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two black-and-white horned rams, and I saw him slaughtering them with his hand, placing his foot upon their sides."
"3249","Ahmad narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to me: from Qatadah: from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted, or: permission was given, to Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf and az-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam to wear silk because of an itch that was in them."
"3250","Ahmad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: from Qatadah: Anas heard him saying: Permission was given to Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf and az-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam to wear a shirt of silk."
"3251","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that Abdur Rahman ibn Awf and az-Zubayr complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lice, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted them to wear shirts of silk. Anas said: I saw each of them wearing a shirt of silk."
"3252","Ahmad narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, he said: When this verse was revealed: {Indeed, We have granted you a clear conquest * That Allah may forgive you your sins, past and future}, the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congratulations to you, O Messenger of Allah, what about us? Then this verse was revealed: {That He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow}. Shubah said: Qatadah used to mention this hadith in his stories, from Anas, he said: This verse was revealed when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from al-Hudaybiyah: {Indeed, We have granted you a clear conquest * That Allah may forgive you}. He said: Then he says: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congratulations to you, O Messenger of Allah, this hadith. He said: So I thought all of it was from Anas. He said: So I came to Kufa and narrated it from Qatadah, from Anas, then I returned and met Qatadah at Wasit, and he was saying: Its beginning is from Anas and its end is from Ikrimah. He said: So I went to them in Kufa and informed them of that."
"3253","Ahmad narrated to us, Shababab narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: {Indeed, We have granted you a clear conquest} was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he returned from al-Hudaybiyah."
"3254","Ahmad narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The moon split twice."
"3255","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, he heard Anas saying: Four people compiled the Quran in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), all of them from the Ansar: Muadh ibn Jabal, Ubayy ibn Kab, Zayd ibn Thabit, and Abu Zayd. Qatadah said: I said to Anas: Who is Abu Zayd? He said: One of my uncles."
"3256","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three qualities, whoever has them finds through them the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger be more beloved to him than anything else, that being thrown into the Fire be more beloved to him than returning to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it, and that he love a person only for the sake of Allah."
"3257","Ahmad narrated to us, Shababab narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."
"3258","And he said: None of you believes until I am more beloved to him than his child, his father, and all people."
"3259","And he said: None of you finds the sweetness of faith until Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else, and until he loves a man only for the sake of Allah, and being thrown into the Fire is more beloved to him than returning to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it."
"3260","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no servant who has goodness with Allah who loves to return to this world except the martyr, for he loves to return and be killed ten times, because of what he sees of the excellence of honor."
"3261","Ahmad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sever ties, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers, as Allah has commanded you."
"3262","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest of people in prayer while completing it."
"3263","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two, like the superiority of one of them over the other."
"3264","Ahmad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Abu at-Tayyah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two, meaning the index finger and the middle finger."
"3265","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, Anas narrated to us, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophet except that he warned his nation of the one-eyed liar. Verily he is one-eyed, and indeed your Lord is not one-eyed; written between his eyes is Kafir, every believer will read it."
"3266","Ahmad narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and I do not know whether something was revealed to him or he was saying it: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth he would wish - or: he would seek - a third valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"3267","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth he would seek a second to it, and if he had a second he would seek a third to it, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents. Anas said: So I do not know whether something was revealed to him or a saying he used to say."
"3268","Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam grows old while two things remain in him: greed and hope."
"3269","Ahmad narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to me, he said: I heard Qatadah ibn Diamah narrating from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord says: When the servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near a cubit, and when he draws near a cubit, I draw near a fathom, and when he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"3270","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, he heard Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Indeed Allah says: If My servant draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit, and if he draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom, and if he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening."
"3271","Ahmad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to the Romans, and it was said to him: They do not accept a letter except with a seal, so he took a ring of silver, as if I am looking at its whiteness on his hand, its engraving: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"3272","Ahmad narrated to us, Shababah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write to the Romans, it was said to him: They will not read a letter if it is not sealed, so he took a ring of silver, and its engraving: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. Anas said: As if I am looking at its whiteness on his hand."
"3273","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah - Abu Dawud said: And Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Hisham said: He will come out of the Fire; Shubah said: Bring out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and in his heart is goodness weighing a wheat grain; bring out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah and in his heart is goodness weighing an atom - and Shubah said: a mote - and there will come out of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah and in his heart is goodness weighing a barley grain."
"3274","Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Thabit informed me, he heard Anas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate often with this supplication: Our Lord, give us good in this world, and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. Shubah said: So I mentioned that to Qatadah, and he said: Anas used to supplicate."
"3275","Abu Nasr Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Qushayri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires."
"3276","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed on a road, and a black woman passed, and a man said to her: Make way, and she said: Make way? Bah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave her, for she is headstrong."
"3277","Abd al-Ala and Hawtharah narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour be established? When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he said: Where is the one asking about the Hour? He said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: It is surely coming, so what have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared for it much deeds, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. So he said: You are with whom you love. He said: And with him was a boy from the Ansar called Muhammad, so he said: If this one lives, old age will not overtake him before the Hour comes. And it is from the copy of Abd al-Ala."
"3278","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people but has not done their deeds? He said: A person is with whom he loves. Hammad said: And he said in the hadith: The Muslims did not rejoice at anything after Islam as they rejoiced at it."
"3279","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three qualities, whoever has them finds the sweetness of faith: whoever has Allah and His Messenger more beloved to him than returning as a Jew or a Christian..."
"3280","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A man loves a people for the good deeds they do, yet he has not done like them? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with whom he loves. Or: with whom he loves. He said: So the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejoiced at that with a joy I never saw them rejoice at anything like it."
"3281","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with whom you love. Anas said: So I love Allah and His Messenger."
"3282","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted continuously in Ramadan, and some of his Companions fasted continuously, so he said: If the month were extended for me, I would fast continuously in a manner that the overzealous would abandon their excess; I spend the night, my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."
"3283","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I took Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah took him while he was in a cloak treating a camel of his with tar, so he said: Do you have dates with you? I said: Yes, so I handed him some dates and he threw them into his mouth and chewed them, then he opened the mouth of the boy and spat it into his mouth, and he began to smack his lips, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The beloved of the Ansar is dates, and he named him Abdullah."
"3284","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Ubaydullah al-Asari narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins from my nation."
"3285","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj as-Sami narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, Anas narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness, and the vision of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"3286","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Muslim, the companion of as-Sabiri, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is like an ear of grain, bending sometimes and standing straight sometimes."
"3287","Hudbah and Hawtharah narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: Send with us a man to teach us. So he took the hands of Abu Ubaydah and sent him with them, and said: This is the trustworthy one of this nation."
"3288","Shayban and Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A son was born to me tonight, and I named him after my father Ibrahim, then I entrusted him to Umm Sayf, the wife of a blacksmith in Madinah. And in the hadith of Shayban: So he went to visit him. And in the hadith of Hudbah: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to visit him and I followed him, and we reached Abu Sayf while he was blowing on his bellows, and the house had filled with smoke, so I hastened walking ahead of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu Sayf, the Messenger of Allah has come, so he stopped. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for the boy, embraced him, and said what Allah willed him to say. He said: I saw him afterward while he was struggling with his soul before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And in the hadith of Hudbah: And the eye of the Messenger of Allah was shedding tears. And in the hadith of Shayban: So the eyes of the Messenger of Allah shed tears. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The eye sheds tears and the heart grieves, and we say only what pleases our Lord. And in the hadith of Shayban: By Allah, we are indeed grieved by you, O Ibrahim. And in the hadith of Hudbah: And we are indeed grieved by you, O Ibrahim."
"3289","Shayban narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, he said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like dreams. Sometimes a man would see a dream and he would ask about him if he did not know him; if he was praised with good, his dream pleased him more for him. Then a woman came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw as if I was brought and taken out of Madinah, and admitted into Paradise, and I heard a thud at which Paradise shook, and I looked and there was so-and-so son of so-and-so, and so-and-so son of so-and-so - she named twelve men; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent an expedition of like that number - and they were brought to them wearing dusty clothes, their jugular veins spurting, and it was said: Take them to the river al-Baydaj, or: al-Bayrah. He said: So they were dipped in it, and they came out with faces like the moon on the night of full moon, and they were brought a platter of gold containing unripe dates, and they ate of its unripe dates as they wished; they did not turn it from any side except they ate of the fruit what they wanted, and I ate with them. Then the bearer of glad tidings came from that expedition and said: Such and such happened in our affair, so-and-so and so-and-so were struck, until he counted twelve men. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the woman and said: Relate your dream. So she related it, saying: So-and-so was brought, and so-and-so was brought, as he had said."
"3290","Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given al-Kawthar; I struck my hand to its soil and it was the most fragrant musk, and its pebbles were pearls, and its banks were domes of pearl."
"3291","Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Straighten the rows - two or three times - by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I see you from behind me as I see you from before me. And Humayd added in the hadith: Straighten the rows and stand close together."
"3292","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: Two men will come out of the Fire and be presented to Allah, and they will be turned toward the Fire - he mentioned something like the hadith of Abd ar-Rahman - and they will be admitted into Paradise."
"3293","Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a young man from Aslam said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to fight in jihad but I have nothing to equip myself with. He said: Go to so-and-so the Ansari, for he had equipped himself; say to him: The Messenger of Allah conveys greetings to you and says to you: Hand over to me what you equipped yourself with. So he came to him, and the man said - I think to his wife: Do not withhold anything of it; by Allah, do not withhold anything of it, so that it will be blessed for us in it."
"3294","Bishr ibn Hilal as-Sawwaf narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to hear the crying of a child while in prayer, so he would recite a short surah and a light surah."
"3295","Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Ghubari narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, something like it. Repeated."
"3296","Bishr narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out to battle with Umm Sulaym, and with her were women from the Ansar, who would give water and treat the wounded."
"3297","Bishr ibn Hilal as-Sawwaf narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the day came on which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Madinah, everything in it lit up; and when the day came on which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, everything in it darkened, and we had not yet shaken the dust off our hands from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - while we were burying him - before we found our hearts changed."
"3298","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj as-Sami narrated to us, Bashshar ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A righteous trait may be in a man, and Allah sets right all his deeds through it; and a man's purification for his prayer - Allah expiates his sins through his purification, and his prayer remains for him as supererogatory."
"3299","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj as-Sami narrated to us, Bashshar ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Abu Dharr and said: O Abu Dharr, shall I not point you to two traits, lighter on the back and heavier in the scale than others? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Upon you is good character and long silence; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, creatures have never adorned themselves with their like."
"3300","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Habib ibn Hajar narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I left the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heading to my family, and I passed by boys, and their play pleased me, so I stood watching the boys. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached me while I was standing over them, and he greeted the boys, then sent me on an errand of his. I returned to my mother later than the time I used to return to them, and my mother said to me: What kept you today, my son? I said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand. She said: What errand? He said: I said: O mother, it is a secret. She said: My son, then guard the secret of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Thabit said: So I said to Anas: O Abu Hamzah, do you remember that errand today - or: do you recall it? He said: I indeed remember it; had I told anyone of it, I would have told you, O Thabit."
"3301","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath Abu Bahr narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: That the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out early at night with waterskins, giving drink to the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3302","Hudbah ibn Khalid and Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud while wiping blood from his face: How can a people prosper who wounded their prophet and broke his tooth while he calls them to Allah? So Allah revealed: {You have no part in the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers}."
"3303","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, so he gave him sheep filling the area between two mountains. The man came to his people and said: O my people, embrace Islam, for by Allah, Muhammad gives the giving of a man who does not fear poverty. And a man would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanting nothing but worldly gain, yet by evening his religion would be more beloved to him than the world and all in it."
"3304","Al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit - he said: I think, from Anas - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a man visiting him in sickness, and found him dying. He greeted him and said: How do you find yourself? He said: Well, O Messenger of Allah; I hope in Allah Almighty, and I fear my sins. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two never combine in the heart of a man at this place except that Allah gives him what he hopes and grants him safety from what he fears."
"3305","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Ghassan ibn Burzin - meaning at-Tuhawi - narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came early one day and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are ruined, by the Lord of the Kabah. He said: What is that? They said: Hypocrisy, hypocrisy. He said: Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? They said: Yes. He said: That is not hypocrisy. He said: Then they returned a second time and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are ruined, by the Lord of the Kabah. He said: What is that? They said: Hypocrisy, hypocrisy. He said: Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? They said: Yes. He said: That is not hypocrisy. He said: Then they returned a third time and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are ruined, by the Lord of the Kabah. He said: What is that? They said: Hypocrisy. He said: Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? They said: Yes. He said: That is not hypocrisy. They said: When we are with you we are in one state, and when we leave you the world and our families preoccupy us. He said: If when you left me you remained in the state you are in with me, the angels would shake hands with you on the roads of Madinah."
"3306","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj as-Sami narrated to us, Abu Thabit Abd al-Wahid ibn Thabit narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like to break fast with three dates, or something untouched by fire."
"3307","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer one night until midnight, then he came out and prayed with them. And he did not mention ablution."
"3308","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raid at dawn prayer, listening for the call to prayer; if he heard a call he desisted, otherwise he raided. One day he listened and heard a man saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the natural faith. He said: I testify that there is no god but Allah. So he said: You have come out of the Fire."
"3309","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then shoot arrows, so one of us could see where his arrow landed."
"3310","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Isha prayer was established one night, and a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need. So he stood with him conversing until the people - or some of the people - dozed, then he stood and prayed. And he did not mention ablution."
"3311","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, something like it."
"3312","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj as-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, Qatadah, and Humayd, from Anas, that some people from Uraynah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found Madinah unhealthy, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them to the charity camels, and ordered them to drink of their urine and milk."
"3313","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he ate food would lick his three fingers, and said: When a morsel of one of you falls, let him remove the harm from it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan. And he ordered us to wipe the dish clean, and said: One of you does not know in which part of his food blessing lies for him."
"3314","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, that they said to Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah have a ring? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer one night until midnight had passed - or: midnight was about to pass - then he came and said: The people have prayed, and you will remain in prayer as long as you wait for prayer. Anas said: As if I am looking at the sparkle of his silver ring. He said: And Anas raised his left hand showing us."
"3315","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went around his wives with a single washing."
"3316","Abu ar-Rabi az-Zahrani narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The creation are the dependents of Allah, so the most beloved of them to Allah are the most beneficial of them to His dependents."
"3317","Hudbah narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whom Allah promises a reward for a deed, He will fulfill it for him; and whom He threatens with punishment for a deed, He has the choice in it."
"3318","Hudbah ibn Khalid and Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, they said: Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding this verse: {He is worthy of fear and worthy of forgiveness}: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord says: I am worthy to be feared so that no other is associated with Me, and I am worthy, for whoever fears Me so as not to associate another with Me, to forgive him."
"3319","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said on the day of Uhud: O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped on earth."
"3320","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud when they pressed him while he was with seven men from the Ansar and two men from Quraysh: Who will repel them from us, and he will be my companion in Paradise? So a man from the Ansar stood and fought until he was killed. Then he said the like of that, and another stood and fought until he was killed. He kept saying the like of that until the seven were killed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have not done justice to our companions."
"3321","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Abu Ubaydah and Abu Talhah."
"3322","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When Allah created Adam, Iblis circled him looking at him; when he saw him hollow, he said: I have prevailed! A creation that cannot control itself."
"3323","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to Badr, pointed with his hand to the ground and said: This is the death-place of so-and-so. By Allah, not one of them deviated from his death-place."
"3324","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he made peace with Quraysh on the day of al-Hudaybiyah, said to Ali: Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Suhayl ibn Amr said: We do not know the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; write: In Your name, O Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Write: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, has agreed upon. Suhayl ibn Amr said: If we knew you were the Messenger of Allah we would have followed you and not denied you; write your lineage from your father. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Write: Muhammad ibn Abdullah. So he wrote: Whoever comes to us from you, we return him to you; and whoever comes to you from us, you leave him with you. They said: O Messenger of Allah, do you give them this? He said: Whoever goes to them from us, Allah has distanced him; and whoever comes to us from them and we return him to them, Allah will make for him relief and a way out."
"3325","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say while digging the trench, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: For the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"3326","Hudbah and Shayban narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I passed by Musa on the night I was taken up, while he was standing praying in his grave near the red dune."
"3327","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the slain of Badr for three days, then came to them and stood over them and called them: O Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, O Umayyah ibn Khalaf, O Utbah ibn Rabiah, O Shaybah ibn Rabiah, have you found what your Lord promised true? For I have found what my Lord promised me true. Umar heard the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, how do they hear, and how can they answer when they have decayed? He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you are not more hearing of what I say than they, except that they cannot answer. Then he ordered them and they were dragged to the well of Badr."
"3328","Hudbah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: I said to Anas: Narrate to me something of these wonders that none but you narrates. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr one day in Madinah, then came to the seats where Jibril used to come to him, and sat on them. Then Bilal came and called for Asr. Those who had families in Madinah rose to perform ablution and relieve themselves, while men from the Muhajirun remained who had no families in Madinah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a cup - meaning a wide one containing water - and he placed his fingers in the cup, but it did not accommodate all his fingers, so he placed these four. He said: Come and perform ablution. So they all performed ablution. I said to Anas: How many do you think they were? He said: Between seventy and eighty."
"3329","Hudbah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, and there was none but I, my mother, and my aunt Umm Haram. He said: Stand, so I may pray for you - and that was outside prayer time. A man said to Thabit: Where did he place Anas? He said: To his right. He said: So he supplicated for us, the people of the house, with every good of this world and the Hereafter. My mother said: O Messenger of Allah, your little servant Anas, supplicate to Allah for him. So he supplicated for me with every good, and the last of what he supplicated for me: O Allah, increase his wealth and children, and bless him in it."
"3330","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water and was brought a wide cup. He said: The people began performing ablution, and I estimated between sixty and eighty. He said: I kept looking at the water gushing from between his fingers."
"3331","Hudbah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I do not recognize anything I knew in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except your saying: There is no god but Allah. He said: It was said: Prayer, O Abu Hamzah? He said: You pray it at sunset; was that the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Yet I have not seen a time better for a worker than this time of yours."
"3332","Hudbah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When this verse was revealed: {O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, nor speak loudly to him}, Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas sat in his house and said: I am the one who used to raise my voice and speak loudly to him, and I am of the people of the Fire. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him and they informed him, so he said: Rather, he is of the people of Paradise. Anas said: We used to see him walking among us while we knew he was of the people of Paradise. When the day of Yamamah came, with that retreat, he wore his clothes, perfumed himself, advanced, and fought until he was killed."
"3333","Hudbah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Thabit said, Anas said: When the waiting period of Zaynab ended, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Zayd: Go to her and mention me to her. He said: So Zayd went to her while she was kneading her dough. He said: She loomed great in my breast, so I could not look at her when I knew the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had mentioned her; I turned my back to her and stepped back on my heels. I said: O Zaynab, glad tidings; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has mentioned you. She said: I will do nothing until I consult my Lord. So she stood to her prayer place, and the Quran was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her without permission. Anas said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) feed us bread and meat on her occasion until the day extended. He said: The people left, and a group remained in the house talking, enjoying the talk. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and I followed him; he visited the rooms of his wives greeting them, and they said: How did you find your family, O Messenger of Allah? I do not know whether I informed him that the people had left, or he was informed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went until he entered the house; I went to enter with him, and he cast the curtain between me and him. And the verse of the veil was revealed, and the people were admonished with what they were admonished with."
"3334","Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, he said: We used to hesitate to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about anything, and we used to like that a desert man come and ask him while we listened. Then a man of them came to him and said: O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and claimed that you claim Allah sent you. He said: He spoke truth. He said: Who created the heaven? He said: Allah. He said: Who created the earth? He said: Allah. He said: Who set up these mountains? He said: Allah. He said: Who placed in them these springs? He said: Allah. He said: By the One Who created the heaven and earth, set up the mountains, and placed in them these springs - has Allah sent you? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed that five prayers are upon us in our day and night. He said: He spoke truth. He said: By the One Who sent you - has Allah commanded you with this? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed that charity is upon us in our wealth? He said: He spoke truth. He said: By the One Who sent you - has Allah commanded you with this? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed that fasting a month in our year is upon us? He said: He spoke truth. He said: By the One Who sent you - has Allah commanded you with this? He said: Yes. He said: Your messenger claimed that pilgrimage to the House is upon whoever can find a way to it? He said: He spoke truth. He said: By the One Who sent you - has Allah commanded you with this? He said: Yes. He said: By the One Who sent you with truth, I will neither add to them nor subtract from them. He said: When he turned away, he said: If he speaks truth, he will enter Paradise."
"3335","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid an-Narsi narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the Friday sermon, and the people stood up to him, shouting: O Prophet of Allah, rain has failed, trees have reddened, livestock have perished; supplicate to Allah to give us drink. He said: O Allah, give us drink; O Allah, give us drink. He said: By Allah, we saw no patch of cloud in the sky; then a cloud formed and spread, then it rained. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended, prayed, and left; it kept raining until the next Friday. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood delivering the sermon, they shouted: O Prophet of Allah, houses have collapsed, roads are cut; supplicate to Allah to withhold it from us. He said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. He said: It cleared away from Madinah, raining around it, while not a drop rained in Madinah. I looked at Madinah, and it was as if in a wreath."
"3336","Musab ibn Abdullah az-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man used to persist in reciting {Say: He is Allah, One} in prayer in every surah while leading his companions. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What compels you to this surah? He said: I love it. He said: Your love of it has admitted you into Paradise."
"3337","Hawtharah ibn Ashras narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I love {Say: He is Allah, One}. He said: Your love of it has admitted you into Paradise."
"3338","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya adh-Dhari narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, indeed the true good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"3339","Abdullah ibn Salamah narrated to us, Imran ibn Khalid al-Khuzai narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to make brotherhood between two of his Companions; the night would seem long to one of them until he met his brother, greeting him with love and gentleness, saying: How were you after me? As for the generality, three days would not pass for one of them without knowing his brother's state."
"3340","Al-Abbas narrated to us, Imran ibn Khalid al-Khuzai narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the house of Aishah, and some of his Companions were awaiting food. He said: She preceded her - Imran said: My strongest thought is that she was Hafsah - with a platter containing tharid. She said: So I placed it. She said: Then Aishah came out and took the bowl - that was before they veiled - He said: So she struck it and it broke. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it, joined it, and said with his hand - Imran demonstrated: joining it - and said: Eat; your mother became jealous. He said: When they finished, he sent the platter to Hafsah, and sent the broken one to Aishah. So it became a ruling: Whoever breaks something, it is his, and upon him is its like."
"3341","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Thabit al-Bahili narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take pre-dawn meal, even with a sip of water."
"3342","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr and others narrated to us, they said: Daylam ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man of his Companions to a chief of the polytheists, calling him to Allah. He said: This god you call to - is he of silver or of copper? His saying weighed heavy in the breast of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Return to him and call him to Allah. So he returned and he said to him the like of his saying. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Return and call him to Allah. And Allah sent a thunderbolt upon him. Then he returned and said to him the like of his saying... then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him that Allah had destroyed his man. And there was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {And He sends thunderbolts and strikes with them whom He wills, while they dispute about Allah}."
"3343","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Ibn Abi Sarah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, something like it."
"3344","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Daylam ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: There was a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Julaybib, with unattractiveness in his face. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered him marriage. He said: Then you will find me unmarketable. He said: But with Allah you are not unmarketable."
"3345","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Daylam ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: There was a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Julaybib, and he mentioned something like it."
"3346","Hawtharah ibn Ashras narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), al-Adba, was unbeaten. Then a Bedouin came with a young camel of his and raced her, and the Bedouin outran her. That weighed heavy on the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: It is a right upon Allah that nothing of this world is raised except that He lowers it."
"3347","Bassam ibn Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, something like it."
"3348","Hawtharah ibn Ashras narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit us, and I had a small brother nicknamed Abu Umayr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: O Abu Umayr, what happened to the little bird?"
"3349","Abu ar-Rabi az-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw yellowness on Abdur Rahman ibn Awf and said: What is this? He said: I married a woman for the weight of a date-stone of gold. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah bless you. Then he said to him: Give a wedding feast, even with a sheep."
"3350","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give a wedding feast for any of his wives like he gave for Zaynab, for he slaughtered a sheep."
"3351","Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu ar-Rabi az-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us - he said: I think, from Anas - he said: There was a Jewish boy serving the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he fell ill. He came to visit him, with his father at his head. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him, and the boy looked at his father. His father said to him: Obey Abu al-Qasim. So he said: I testify that there is no god but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Then the boy died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out saying: Praise be to Allah Who saved him through me from the Fire."
"3352","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"3353","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A funeral passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they praised it with good, so he said: It has become due. And another funeral passed and they praised it with evil, so he said: It has become due. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, you said for this one: It has become due, and for this one: It has become due. He said: Due to the testimony of the people."
"3354","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, the like of it, and he added in it: And you are the witnesses of Allah on earth."
"3355","Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sallam narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a Persian man was a neighbor of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his broth was the sweetest-smelling thing. He prepared food then invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Aishah beside him. He said: So he gestured to him: Come. He said: And this one with me? And he pointed to Aishah. He said: No. Then he gestured to him a second time, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And this one with me? He said: No. Then he said a third time, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, pointing to Aishah: Yes."
"3356","Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad said: O Abu Hamzah, did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention the Pool? He said: I left in Madinah old women who often ask Allah to bring them to the pool of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3357","Hawtharah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made an alliance between the Ansar and the Muhajirun in the house of Anas in Madinah."
"3358","And Murrah narrated it to us another time, from Asim, from Anas."
"3359","Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Space will remain in Paradise as long as Allah wills it to remain, then Allah will create for it a creation as He wills."
"3360","Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Abu Imran, from Anas, he said: There will come out of the Fire - Abu Imran said: four, and Thabit said: two men - and they will be presented to their Lord, and they will be ordered to the Fire. One of them will turn and say: My Lord! I had hoped that if You took me out of it, You would not return me to it. So Allah will save him from it."
"3361","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I never prayed behind anyone briefer in prayer, while completing it, than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); his prayer was moderate, and the prayer of Abu Bakr was moderate. When Umar came, he lengthened the dawn prayer. And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, he would stand until we said: He has forgotten. Then he would prostrate, and sit between the two prostrations until we said: He has forgotten."
"3362","Hudbah narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I used to serve drink to Abu Ubaydah, Abu Talhah, Ubayy ibn Kab, Simak ibn Kharashah, and Suhayl ibn Bayda - a mixture of ripe and unripe dates - until it took effect in them. Then a man passed calling: Verily wine has been forbidden. He said: So they said: O Anas, overturn your vessel. By Allah, they did not wait to know whether he was truthful or lying; by Allah, it never returned to their heads before they met Allah."
"3363","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I was the cupbearer of the people on the day wine was forbidden, in the house of Abu Talhah; their drink was only fadikh - unripe and ripe dates. Then a caller called: Verily wine has been forbidden. He said: So it flowed in the streets of Madinah. Abu Talhah said: Go out and spill it. He said: So I spilled it. They said - or some of them said: So-and-so was killed and so-and-so was killed while it was in their bellies - I do not know whether it is from the hadith of Anas - He said: So Allah revealed: {There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted} the verse."
"3364","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: Anas said to us: I do my best to pray with you as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying with us. Thabit said: I saw Anas doing something I do not see you doing: when he raised his head from bowing he would stand until one would say: He has forgotten; and when he raised his head from the first prostration he would pause until one would say: He has forgotten."
"3365","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: Anas was asked about the dyeing of the Messenger of Allah, and he said: Had I wished to count the white hairs on his head I would have done so. And he said: He did not dye, while Abu Bakr dyed with henna and katam, and Umar dyed with henna."
"3366","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Hatim ibn Maymun narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites in a day {Say: He is Allah, One} two hundred times, fifteen hundred good deeds are written for him, unless he has a debt upon him."
"3367","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand, and I passed by boys, so I sat with them and was delayed from him. He came out and saw me with the boys, and greeted them."
"3368","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years, and he never said to me: Uff, ever; nor did he say of anything a servant did: Why did you do such and such, or: Why did you not do such and such."
"3369","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, al-Harith narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: O so-and-so, did you do such and such? He said: No, by Allah besides Whom there is no god, I did not do it, while the Messenger of Allah knew he had done it. So he said to him: Allah has expiated your lie for you through your testifying: There is no god but Allah."
"3370","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are with you in one state, but when we part from you we are in another. He said: How are you with your Prophet? They said: You are our Prophet in secret and in public. He said: That is not hypocrisy of you."
"3371","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The creation are the dependents of Allah, so the most beloved of them to Allah are the most beneficial of them to His dependents."
"3372","Abu ar-Rabi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with these supplications in the morning and evening: O Allah, I ask You of sudden good, and I seek refuge in You from sudden evil; for a servant does not know what will befall him suddenly in the morning or evening."
"3373","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely will be given it, even if it does not strike him."
"3374","Shayban narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, raised to the Prophet: Yusuf was given half of beauty."
"3375","Shayban narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Jibril came to him while he was playing with the boys - took him, threw him down, split his heart, and extracted a clot from it. He said: This is the share of Satan from you. Then he washed it in a basin of gold with Zamzam water, then joined it, then returned it to its place. The boys came running to his mother - meaning his foster mother - saying: Muhammad has been killed. She met him pale in color. Anas said: I used to see the trace of that stitching on his chest."
"3376","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was brought al-Buraq - a white, tall animal, above a donkey and below a mule - placing its hoof at the limit of its sight. He said: So I rode it until I came to Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: So I tied it to the ring to which the prophets tie. Then I entered the mosque and prayed in it two rakahs, then I came out."
"3377","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Jushami narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the crying of a child with his mother in prayer, he would recite a light surah, or: a short surah. Jafar doubted."
"3378","Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd ar-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lick his three fingers when he ate, and said: When a morsel of one of you falls, let him remove what harm is on it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan; and let him wipe the dish clean, for you do not know in which of your food the blessing lies."
"3379","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: When the day came on which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, everything in it lit up; and when the day came on which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, everything in it darkened. He said: And we had not yet shaken our hands of the dust of the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before we found our hearts changed."
"3380","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Fatimah said to me: O Anas, how could your hearts bear to throw dust upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?!"
"3381","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grew heavy in illness, he would stretch one leg and draw in another, and stretch one hand and draw in another. Fatimah said: O my distress for your distress, O my father - al-Qawariri said: Hammad said: Memorize; he said: O my distress, and did not say: O my distress for your distress, O my father - The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My little daughter, there is no distress upon your father after today. When he passed away, Fatimah said: O my father, he answered a Lord Who called him; O my father, to Jibril we announce him! O my father, how near he is to his Lord! O my father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode. Anas said: When we buried him, Fatimah said to me: O Anas, how could your hearts bear to throw dust upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"3382","Abu Hamzah Huraym ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father mentioning from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When there was revealed: {O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet} to His saying: {while you perceive not}, Thabit ibn Qays said: I, by Allah, am the one who used to raise my voice near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I fear I am of the people of the Fire; I used to raise my voice near the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather, he is of the people of Paradise. Or as he said."
"3383","Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Shubah, from Thabit, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every treacherous one there is a banner."
"3384","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abu Jumay al-Hujaymi narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Ali and Fatimah a servant boy and said: Treat him well, for I saw him praying."
"3385","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd ar-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver sermons leaning on a palm trunk. When the pulpit was built, he preached upon the pulpit, and the trunk moaned. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it and embraced it. He said: Had I not embraced it, it would have moaned until the Day of Resurrection."
"3386","Abu Musa Harun ibn Abdullah al-Hammal narrated to us, Abu Dawud at-Tayalisi narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Umm Salamah for household goods worth ten dirhams."
"3387","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Dawud at-Tayalisi narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You name them Muhammad then you curse them?!"
"3388","Harun ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come out to the mosque where the Muhajirun and Ansar were, none of them raising his head from his hunched sitting except Abu Bakr and Umar, for he would smile at them and they would smile at him."
"3389","Harun narrated to us, Abu Dawud at-Tayalisi narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Atiyyah, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I hope to meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Resurrection and say: O Messenger of Allah, your little servant."
"3390","Harun narrated to us, Abu Dawud at-Tayalisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, from Abu Talhah, that he entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the illness in which he died, and he said to me: Convey greetings to your people, and inform them that they - as far as I know - are chaste and patient."
"3391","Al-Fadl ibn as-Sabbah Abu al-Abbas narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, from Muhtasib, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When shall I meet my brothers? They said: O Messenger of Allah, are we not your brothers? He said: Rather you are my companions; my brothers are those who believed in me and did not see me."
"3392","Al-Fadl ibn as-Sabbah narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, from Muhtasib, from Thabit, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessed is he who saw me and believed in me, once; and blessed is he who did not see me and believed in me, seven times."
"3393","Al-Fadl ibn as-Sabbah narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, from Muhtasib, from Thabit, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I sit with people remembering Allah after the dawn prayer until the sun rises is more beloved to me than freeing four of the sons of Ismail, the blood-money of each of them twelve thousand; and that I sit with people remembering Allah after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets is more beloved to me than freeing four of the sons of Ismail, the blood-money of each of them twelve thousand."
"3394","Al-Muqaddami Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, the brother of Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, the people looked up at him, and he lowered his head upon his saddle in humility."
"3395","Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, the people of Makkah stood in two rows. He said: And Abdullah ibn Rawahah was saying: ... He said: So Umar said: O Ibn Rawahah, do you recite poetry before the Messenger of Allah, and in the sanctuary of Allah? He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hush, O Umar; this is harder upon them than the falling of arrows."
"3396","Abu Musa narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn 'Umarah al-Dhari' narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit narrating from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say on the Day of the Trench:"
"3397","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: the sister of al-Rubayyi', Umm Harithah, wounded a person, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Retaliation, retaliation. So Umm al-Rubayyi' said: O Messenger of Allah, will retaliation be exacted from so-and-so? No, by Allah, it shall not be exacted from her. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah, O Umm al-Rubayyi', retaliation is the decree of Allah. She said: No, by Allah, it shall never be exacted from her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the servants of Allah are those who, if they swear an oath by Allah, Allah fulfills it for them."
"3398","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit: they said to Anas: Supplicate for us. So he said: O Allah, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. They said: Give us more. So he repeated it. They said: Give us more. He said: What do you want? I have asked for you the good of this world and the Hereafter. Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate often: O Allah, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"3399","Shayban narrated to us, 'Umarah ibn Zadhan narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas: Abu Talhah had a son nicknamed Abu 'Umayr. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Abu 'Umayr, what did the little bird do? He said: Then the boy was taken while Abu Talhah was away in one of his gardens, and the child died. So Umm Sulaym stood, washed him, shrouded him, covered him with a cloth, and said: Let no one inform Abu Talhah until I am the one to inform him. Then Abu Talhah came, exhausted, while fasting. So she perfumed herself and adorned herself for him, and brought his dinner. He said: What happened to Abu 'Umayr? She said: He is at rest. So he ate dinner, and had from her what a man has from his wife. Then she said: O Abu Talhah, tell me: a household that lent another household a loaned item, then its owners asked for it back, should they return it or withhold it? He said: Rather they should return it to them. So she said: Then seek reward with Allah for Abu 'Umayr. He said: So he became angry, and set out as he was to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of Umm Sulaym's words and deed. So he said: May Allah bless for you two the latter part of your night. He said: So she conceived 'Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, and when she delivered him, on the seventh day Umm Sulaym said to me: O Anas, take this boy to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this basket contains some 'Ajwah dates, so that he himself may do his tahnik and name him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stretched his legs, laid him in his lap, took a date, chewed it, and put it in the boy's mouth, and the boy began to smack his lips. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ansar insist on nothing but love of dates."
"3400","Shayban narrated to us, 'Umarah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked pumpkin, which is gourd."
"3401","Shayban narrated to us, 'Umarah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: I never touched with this palm of mine anything softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): neither silk nor ambergris, and other things he mentioned which I do not remember. And I never found a scent more pleasant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And I accompanied him for ten years, and he never said to me about anything at all: Why did you do such-and-such?"
"3402","Shayban narrated to us, 'Umarah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The caller to prayer, or Bilal, would call the iqamah, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter, and a man would meet him and stand with him until most of them nodded off with their heads."
"3403","Shayban narrated to us, 'Umarah ibn Zadhan narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The angel of rain asked his Lord for permission to visit the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so He permitted him, and it was the day of Umm Salamah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umm Salamah, guard the door for us; let no one enter upon us. He said: While she was at the door, al-Husayn ibn 'Ali came and pushed his way in, opened the door, and entered. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to embrace him and kiss him. So the angel said: Do you love him? He said: Yes. He said: Your nation will kill him; if you wish I will show you the place where they will kill him. He said: Yes. He said: So he took a handful from the place where he would be killed and showed him; then some soft red soil came, and Umm Salamah took it and placed it in her garment. Thabit said: So we used to say: It is Karbala."
"3404","Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Ghubari narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let each one of you ask his Lord for all his needs, even the strap of his sandal if it breaks."
"3405","Qatan ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood among his companions: he joined Salman with Abu al-Darda', and he joined 'Awf ibn Malik with Sa'b ibn Jathamah."
"3406","Mu'adh ibn Shu'bah, a Basran, narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Matar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be good neighbors to the blessings of Allah; do not drive them away, for rarely do they depart from a people and then return to them."
"3407","Ibrahim al-Nili narrated to us, Salih, meaning al-Murri, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those who keep the houses of Allah inhabited are the people of Allah."
"3408","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Here I am, for Hajj and 'Umrah together."
"3409","Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, Rushayd Abu 'Abdullah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a gathering of Banu Salimah and said: O Banu Salimah, who is the childless one among you? They said: The one who has no child. He said: Rather, he is the one who has no predecessor. He said: Who is the destitute among you? They said: The one who has no wealth. He said: Rather, he is the one who arrives before Allah with no good to his credit with Allah."
"3410","Sa'id narrated to us, Rushayd narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by the young girls of Banu al-Najjar while they were beating the tambourine and saying: — So the Prophet of Allah said: O Allah, bless them."
"3411","Abu Musa narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn 'Umarah al-Dhari' narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit narrating from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say on the Day of the Trench:"
"3412","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: Umm Sulaym was with Abu Talhah on the day of Khaybar, and she had a dagger with her. So Abu Talhah said to her: O Umm Sulaym, what is this? She said: A dagger I have taken, so that if one of the polytheists comes near me I will rip open his belly with it. Abu Talhah said: O Messenger of Allah, do you not hear what Umm Sulaym says? She says such-and-such, something that eluded Abu Harb, that she will kill them. So he said: Allah has sufficed and done good."
"3413","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: Abu Talhah al-Ansari, on the day of Uhud, was shooting arrows before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the Messenger of Allah behind him. Abu Talhah was a skilled archer, and whenever he shot, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his figure to see where his arrow landed."
"3414","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: Abu Talhah recited Surah Bara'ah, and when he came to this verse: March forth, light and heavy, he said: Do I not see my Lord calling me to march, young and old? Equip me. So his sons said to him: You raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he passed away, and you raided with Abu Bakr until he died, and you raided with 'Umar, so we will raid on your behalf. He said: Equip me. So they equipped him, and he boarded a ship and died, and they found no island on which to bury him except after seven days, and he had not changed."
"3415","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah while 'Abdullah ibn Salam was among his date-palms. When he heard of him, he came and said: I will ask you about things which none knows but a prophet; if you inform me of them, then you are the Messenger of Allah. So he asked him about resemblance, about the first thing that will gather mankind, and about the first thing the people of Paradise will eat. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril informed me of them just now. He said: That is the enemy of the Jews. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for resemblance: when the man's fluid precedes the woman's fluid, the resemblance goes to him, and when the woman's fluid precedes the man's fluid, the resemblance goes to her. The first thing to gather mankind is a fire that will come from the east and gather people toward the west. And the first thing the people of Paradise will eat is the extra lobe of a whale's liver. So 'Abdullah ibn Salam believed. He said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a slanderous people; if they hear of my Islam they will slander me and attack me. So hide me, send for them, and ask them about me. So he sent for them and they came, and he had hidden him, and he said: What kind of man is 'Abdullah ibn Salam among you? They said: Our best and the son of our best, our master and the son of our master, our scholar and the son of our scholar. So he said: What would you think if he believed, would you believe? They said: May Allah protect him from doing that. So he said: Come out, O Ibn Salam, to them. So he came out and said: I testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. So they said: Rather he is our worst and the son of our worst, our ignorant one and the son of our ignorant one. So he said: Did I not tell you, O Messenger of Allah, that they are a slanderous people."
"3416","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Abu Raja' al-Kalbi narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas: The women came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the men have taken the merit: they perform jihad and we do not perform jihad. So he said: The household work of one of you in her house attains the jihad of the mujahidin, Allah willing."
"3417","Nasr ibn 'Ali al-Jahdami and Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, both saying: Abu Raja' Rawh ibn al-Musayyib al-Kalbi narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The women came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the men have taken the merit through jihad in the path of Allah; so what deed is ours by which we may attain the deed of the mujahidin in the path of Allah? He said: The household work of one of you in her house attains the deed of the mujahidin in the path of Allah."
"3418","al-Hasan ibn 'Umar ibn Shaqiq al-Jarmi narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: I think, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a man of the Ansar to visit him in illness, and found him at death. So he greeted him and said: How do you find yourself, O so-and-so? He said: Well, O Messenger of Allah; I hope in Allah and I fear my sins. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two never combine in a man's heart at this moment except that Allah grants him what he hopes and secures him from what he fears."
"3419","al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn Zadhan, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: The king of Dhu Yazan gifted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a suit that had been bought for thirty-three camels."
"3420","'Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two men ever loved one another for the sake of Allah except that the better of the two is the one with stronger love for his companion."
"3421","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Khunays, from Sadaqah, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cares for his Muslim brother's hunger and feeds him until he is full and gives him drink until he is quenched, Allah forgives him."
"3422","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Dhari' narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, true good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"3423","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Sinan Abu 'Awn narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah took a handful and said: To Paradise, by My mercy; and He took a handful and said: To the Fire, and I do not care."
"3424","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was harmed in Allah's cause as no one was harmed, and I was frightened in Allah's cause as no one was frightened, and there passed over me three days of day and night when neither I nor Bilal had any food except what Bilal's armpit concealed."
"3425","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man being supported between his two sons. So he said: What is wrong with him? They said: He vowed to perform Hajj on foot. He said: Allah is in no need of this one's walking; let him ride."
"3426","Abu al-Jahm al-Azraq ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, al-Mustalim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prophets are alive in their graves, praying."
"3427","Qatan ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: Rain fell upon us while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered himself to it and said: It has recently come from its Lord."
"3428","Qatan ibn Nusayr Abu 'Abbad narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas was the orator of the Ansar. When this verse was revealed: O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, nor speak loudly to him as you speak loudly to one another, to the end of the verse, Thabit said: I am the one who used to raise my voice above the voice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I am among the people of the Fire. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather he is among the people of Paradise, rather he is among the people of Paradise."
"3429","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would prostrate, then al-Hasan or al-Husayn would come and ride upon his back, so he would prolong the prostration. It would be said: O Prophet of Allah, you have prolonged the prostration. So he would say: My son has made me his mount, and I disliked hurrying him."
"3430","Abu al-Jahm al-Azraq ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed a man among his brothers for three days, he would ask about him: if he was absent he would supplicate for him, if he was present he would visit him, and if he was ill he would visit him in illness. Then he missed a man of the Ansar on the third day, so he asked about him, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, we left him like a fledgling: nothing enters his head but it exits from his rear. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to some of his companions: Visit your brother in illness. He said: So we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to visit him, and among the people were Abu Bakr and 'Umar. When we entered upon him, he was as described to us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How do you find yourself? He said: Nothing enters my head but it exits from my rear. He said: And why is that? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I passed by you while you were praying Maghrib, so I prayed with you while you were reciting this surah: The Striking Hour, what is the Striking Hour, to its end: A blazing Fire. He said: So I said: O Allah, whatever sin of mine You would punish me for in the Hereafter, hasten its punishment for me in this world. So there befell me what you see. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an evil thing you said; why did you not ask Allah to grant you good in this world and good in the Hereafter and to shield you from the punishment of the Fire? He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him, and he supplicated with that, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for him. He said: So he rose as if released from bonds. He said: When we went out, 'Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, just now you urged us to visit the sick, so what is in it for us? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a Muslim man leaves his house to visit his sick Muslim brother, he wades through mercy up to his waist; then when he sits with the sick one, mercy envelops him and envelops the sick one; the sick one is in the shade of His Throne, and the visitor is in the shade of His sanctity; and Allah says to His angels: See how long the visitors stayed with the sick one. He said: They say: O Lord, a moment, if they stayed a moment, so Allah says to His angels: Write for My visiting servant the worship of a thousand years: its nights spent in prayer and its days in fasting, and inform him that I have not recorded a single sin against him. He said: And He says to His angels: See how long they stayed? He said: They say: An hour. He said: If they stayed an hour, then He says: Write for him an age, and an age is ten thousand years. If he dies before that, he enters Paradise; if he lives, not a single sin is recorded against him. If it is morning, seventy thousand angels pray for him until evening, and he is among the fruits of Paradise; and if it is evening, seventy thousand angels pray for him until morning, and he is among the fruits of Paradise."
"3431","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A believer's dream is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"3432","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Musa narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the best fasting. He said: Sha'ban, in veneration of Ramadan."
"3433","'Abdullah ibn 'Awn al-Kharraz narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pass by the gardens of Paradise, graze. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the gardens of Paradise? He said: Circles of remembrance."
"3434","'Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Mustawrid Abu Hammam narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have left no sin, minor or major, but I have committed it. He said: Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? Three times. He said: Yes. He said: That covers all that."
"3435","Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, al-Azwar ibn Ghalib al-Basri narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani and Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has, on every Friday, six hundred thousand freed ones whom He frees from the Fire. One of the two said in his narration: all of them having deserved the Fire."
"3436","Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, Abu Maymun, a shaykh of the people of Basra, narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has, in every hour of the hours of this world, six hundred thousand freed ones whom He frees from the Fire, all of whom had deserved the Fire."
"3437","Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Ghubari narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hear a child's crying and would recite a short surah."
"3438","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah said to her: A Jew's daughter. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while she was weeping and said: What makes you weep? She said: Hafsah said to me: I am a Jew's daughter. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are the daughter of a prophet, your uncle is a prophet, and you are under a prophet, so in what does she boast over you? Then he said: Fear Allah, O Hafsah."
"3439","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah wanted to marry a woman, so he mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: Go and look at her, for it is more likely to create affection between you two. He said: So he did, married her, and mentioned her compatibility."
"3440","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, Qatadah, and Aban, all from Anas, he said: When wine was prohibited, he said: On that day I was serving eleven men. He said: So they ordered me and I poured it out, and the people poured out their vessels with what was in them, until the streets were nearly blocked by its smell. Anas said: Their wine on that day was only unripe dates and ripe dates mixed. He said: Then a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I had an orphan's wealth with me, and I bought wine with it; do you think I may sell it and return the orphan's wealth to him? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah fight the Jews: fat was prohibited to them, yet they sold it and consumed its price. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not permit him to sell wine."
"3441","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah in 'Umrat al-Qada', with Ibn Rawahah before him, saying: befriend the close friend. 'Umar said to him: O Ibn Rawahah, in the sanctuary of Allah and before the Messenger of Allah you say this poetry? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him alone, O 'Umar, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, his words are harder upon them than the striking of arrows."
"3442","Nasr ibn 'Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr al-Bahili narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt the agony of death that he felt, Fatimah said: O the distress of my father! So he said: No distress upon your father after today; there has come to your father what Allah will not spare anyone from: meeting Him on the Day of Resurrection."
"3443","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I love so-and-so for the sake of Allah. He said: Have you informed him? He said: No. He said: Then go to him and inform him. He said: So he went to him and informed him, saying: O so-and-so, I love you for the sake of Allah. He said: May the One for Whose sake you loved me love you."
"3444","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Bazi' Abu al-Khalil narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hears of a virtue from Allah and does not believe in it will not attain it."
"3445","al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt something, and when morning came it was said: O Messenger of Allah, the trace of pain upon you is evident. He said: Despite what you see of me, last night I recited the seven long surahs."
"3446","al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, from Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said in his address: There is no faith for one with no trustworthiness, and no religion for one with no covenant."
"3447","al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Hammad, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sincerely asks for martyrdom from his heart, Allah grants him the reward of a martyr even if he dies in his bed."
"3448","Shayban narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When I was taken up to the seventh heaven, I saw Ibrahim leaning his back against the Frequented House, into which seventy thousand angels enter every day and never return to it."
"3449","Shayban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Burjumi narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has three daughters or three sisters, fears Allah regarding them, and maintains them, will be with me in Paradise like this, and he gestured with the index and middle fingers."
"3450","Shayban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, he said: I said to Anas: O Anas, inform me of the most amazing thing you saw. He said: Yes, O Thabit. I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years, and he never blamed me for anything I did wrong. When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Zaynab bint Jahsh, my mother said to me: O Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has become a bridegroom, and I do not know whether he has breakfast for him; bring that leather butter-container. So I brought her the container with dates, and she made hays for him. She said: O Anas, take this to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his wife. When I brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a stone bowl containing that hays, he said: Place it in a corner of the house, and invite for me Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Ali, 'Uthman, a group of his companions, then invite for me the people of the mosque and whomever you see on the road. He said: So I kept wondering at the small amount of food and the large number he ordered me to invite, but I disliked disobeying him, until the house and the room were filled. He said: O Anas, do you see anyone left? I said: No, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Bring that bowl. So I brought it and placed it before him; he dipped three fingers into the bowl, and the bowl kept growing and rising, and they kept eating and leaving, until when all had finished and there remained in the bowl about as much as I had brought, he said: Place it before Zaynab. Then I went out and closed a door of palm stalks. Thabit said: I said to Anas: How many do you think ate from that bowl? He said to me: I counted seventy-one or seventy-two."
"3451","Shayban narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When I was taken up to the seventh heaven, I was brought to the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary; its leaves were like elephants' ears and its fruits like jars. When it was covered by Allah's command with what covered it, it changed, and no one among people can describe its beauty. Then He revealed to me what He revealed."
"3452","Shayban narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, one good deed is recorded for him; if he does it, ten are recorded for him. Whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is recorded against him; if he does it, one evil deed is recorded against him."
"3453","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes descend from the minbar after the prayer had been called, and a man would intercept him and speak to him at length, then he would advance to his place of prayer."
"3454","'Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Sinan al-'Abdi narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah took a handful and said: To Paradise, by My mercy; and He took a handful and said: To the Fire, and I do not care."
"3455","Musa ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Thabit, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a grave."
"3456","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit saying: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say often: O Allah, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. Shu'bah said: So I mentioned that to Qatadah, and he said: Anas used to supplicate with this supplication."
"3457","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas: A desert man named Zahir used to bring gifts from the desert to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would equip him when he wanted to leave. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zahir is our desert and we are his town. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved him, and he was an unattractive man. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him while he was selling his goods and embraced him from behind while the man could not see him. So he said: Let go, who is this? Then he recognized the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and kept pressing until he pressed his back against the Prophet's belly once he recognized him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began saying: Who will buy the slave? So the man said: O Messenger of Allah, then you will find me unsellable. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But with Allah you are not unsellable. Or he said: With Allah you are precious."
"3458","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Khalaf narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, raising the narration: Fever is a blast from the blasts of Hell; whoever is afflicted with any of it, it is his share of the Fire."
"3459","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: I heard Anas saying to a woman of his household: Do you know so-and-so? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by her while she was weeping over a grave, and said to her: Fear Allah and be patient. She said: Away from me, for you do not care about my calamity, and she did not know him. It was said to her: He is the Messenger of Allah! So she was seized as if by death. Then she came to his door and found no doorkeeper at it, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not know you. So he said to her: Patience is at the first shock."
"3460","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, the Abyssinians played with their spears in joy at that."
"3461","Ishaq narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached to the middle of his ears."
"3462","Ishaq narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you wish for death."
"3463","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I was serving drink to the people in Abu Talhah's house on the day wine was prohibited; their drink that day was fadikh: unripe and ripe dates, and among them were men of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then a caller called, and he said to me: Go out and look. So I went out, and there was a caller announcing: Wine has been prohibited. He said: It flowed through the streets of Madinah. So I came and informed Abu Talhah. He said: Go out and spill it. One of the people said: So-and-so and so-and-so were killed while it was in their bellies. So Allah revealed: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they tasted, to the end of the verse."
"3464","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a trace of yellow dye and said: What is this? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I married a woman for the weight of a date-stone of gold. He said: May Allah bless for you; give a wedding feast even with a sheep."
"3465","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give a wedding feast for any of his wives as he did for Zaynab, for he slaughtered a sheep."
"3466","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: And what have you prepared for the Hour? He said: Nothing, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with those you love. Anas said: We never rejoiced in anything after Islam as we rejoiced in the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: You are with those you love. He said: So I love the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and 'Umar, and I hope to be with them through my love for them, even though I do not act as they act."
"3467","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people praised it with good, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is confirmed. Then another passed and it was praised with evil, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is confirmed. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, you said of this one it is confirmed and of that one it is confirmed? He said: The testimony of the people; the believers are Allah's witnesses on earth."
"3468","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: I think, from Anas: A Bedouin urinated in the mosque, so some of the people leapt up. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not interrupt him. Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over it."
"3469","Ishaq narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Abi Sarah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once sent a man to one of the pharaohs of the Arabs, saying: Go and call him to me. He said: O Messenger of Allah, he is too defiant for that. He said: Go and call him to me. He said: So he went to him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calls you. He said to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah: And what is Allah? Is He of gold? Is He of silver? Is He of copper? He said: So he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, I told you he is too defiant for that; he said to me such-and-such. He said: Go back to him a second time. He said to him the like of it, and returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, I told you he is too defiant for that. He said: Go back to him and call him. So he returned to him a third time. He said: He repeated that speech to him, and while he was speaking to him, Allah sent a cloud over his head; it thundered, and a thunderbolt fell from it and took off the top of his skull. So Allah revealed: And He sends thunderbolts and strikes with them whom He wills, to the end of the verse."
"3470","Huraym ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from 'Itban ibn Malik, he said: I met 'Itban after that and he narrated to me, and it pleased me, so I said to my son: Write it, and he wrote it. 'Itban said, and his sight had gone: I said: O Prophet of Allah, if you would come to me and pray at my place in a spot I would take as a mosque. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and began praying, while his companions talked among themselves. He said: We mentioned what we suffer of harm from the hypocrites, and they laid most of that upon Malik ibn Dukhshum, and they wished the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be carried to invoke against him so Allah would destroy him. They said: O Prophet of Allah, his affair is such-and-such. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: He says that only with his tongue, with no sincerity in his heart. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah but Allah admits him, or he said: the Fire consumes him, never. Mu'tamir said: My father said: I heard it from Anas, and I never narrated it to anyone."
"3471","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with one of his wives when a man passed by him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She is my wife so-and-so. He said: O Prophet of Allah, of whom I might have thought it, I would not have thought it of you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan flows through the son of Adam like blood."
"3472","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Adhrami narrated to us, Abu Qatan narrated to us, Mubarak narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: I never saw a man whisper into the ear of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he moves his head away until the man moves his head away. I never saw anyone take the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he lets go of his hand until the man is the one to let go of his hand. I never touched anything softer than the skin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I never found a scent more pleasant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3473","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: A woman who had something wrong in her mind said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need of you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O mother of so-and-so, take whichever road you wish, stand in it until I stand with you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed alone with her, conversing with her until she fulfilled her need."
"3474","Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated a narration, and we never rejoiced in anything since we knew Islam more than our rejoicing in it. He said: The believer is rewarded for removing harm from the road, for guiding to the path, for expressing on behalf of one who lisps, and for lending milk, to the extent that he is rewarded for goods tied in his garment which he feels for and his hand misses."
"3475","Abu Hammam narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ma'mar informed me, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had locks reaching to the middle of his ears."
"3476","Abu Yasir 'Ammar ibn Nasr narrated to us, Yusuf ibn 'Atiyyah narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is like the ear of grain: it bends at times and stands straight at times. And the likeness of my nation is like rain: it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."
"3477","Abu Yasir 'Ammar narrated to us, Yusuf narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not honor our elder and mercy our young."
"3478","'Ammar narrated to us, Yusuf narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: A funeral was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him to pray over it. He said: Is there a debt upon him? They said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril forbade me to pray over a man with a debt upon him, and said: The debtor is held in his grave until his debt is settled for him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused to pray over him."
"3479","Abu Yasir narrated to us, Yusuf ibn 'Atiyyah narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Creation are the dependents of Allah, so the most beloved of His creation to Him are the most beneficial to His dependents."
"3480","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, al-Hajjaj ibn 'Ilat said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth in Makkah, and I have family there, and I wish to go to them, so am I free to speak against you or say anything? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him to say what he wished. He said: So he went to his wife when he arrived and said: Gather what you have, for I wish to buy from the spoils of Muhammad and his companions, for they have been plundered and their wealth taken. He said: That spread in Makkah, grieving the Muslims, while the polytheists displayed joy and delight. The news reached al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, and he became crippled in his sitting place, unable to stand. Ma'mar said: al-Jazari informed me, from Miqsam, he said: al-'Abbas took a son of his called Qutham, who resembled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he lay back and placed him upon his chest, saying: Qutham the handsome. Ma'mar said: Thabit said: Anas said: Then he sent a slave of his to al-Hajjaj ibn 'Ilat, saying: Woe to you, what have you brought? What are you saying? What Allah has promised is better than what you have brought. Al-Hajjaj said to his slave: Convey greetings to Abu al-Fadl, and tell him: Let him empty one of his houses for me to come to him, for the news is as will delight him. So his slave came, and when he reached the door he said: Glad tidings, Abu al-Fadl. So al-'Abbas leapt in joy until he kissed between his eyes, and he informed him of what al-Hajjaj said, so he freed him. Then al-Hajjaj came and informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had conquered Khaybar, taken their wealth as spoils, Allah's shares were distributed in their wealth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose Safiyyah bint Huyayy for himself, taking her for himself, giving her choice between freeing her so she would be his wife or rejoining her family, and she chose that he free her and she be his wife. But I came for what I had here; I wished to gather it and take it away, so I asked the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permission and he permitted me to say what I wished, so conceal it from me for three days, then mention what you please. He said: So his wife gathered what she had of jewelry and goods, gathered it, and handed it to him, then he proceeded with it. When three days had passed, al-'Abbas went to al-Hajjaj's wife and said: What did your husband do? She informed him that he had gone, saying: May Allah not grieve you, Abu al-Fadl; what reached you grieved us. He said: Yes, may Allah not grieve me; by Allah's praise it was nothing but what we loved: al-Hajjaj informed me that Allah granted Khaybar to His Messenger, Allah's shares were distributed in it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose Safiyyah for himself. If you need your husband, join him. She said: I think by Allah you are truthful. He said: I am truthful, and the affair is as I informed you. He said: Then he went to the gatherings of Quraysh, who were saying: Nothing befalls you but good, Abu al-Fadl. He said: Nothing befell me but good, by Allah's praise: al-Hajjaj informed me that Allah granted Khaybar to His Messenger, Allah's shares were distributed in it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose Safiyyah for himself, and he asked me to conceal it from him for three days; he only came to take what was his and then leave. He said: So Allah turned the grief that was upon the Muslims onto the polytheists, and those Muslims who had entered their houses grieving came out until they came to al-'Abbas, and Allah returned whatever grief, rage, or disgrace there was onto the polytheists."
"3481","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, and Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He heard voices and said: What are these voices? They said: The palm trees, they are pollinating them. He said: If they did not do it, it would still be fine. He said: So they refrained and did not pollinate that year, and it became poor unripe dates. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If it is a matter of your worldly affairs, then it is up to you, and if it is something of your religious affairs, then refer it to me."
"3482","Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who dies and four households among his nearest neighbors testify that they know nothing of him except good, except that Allah says: I have accepted your knowledge, and I have forgiven him what you do not know."
"3483","Ammar Abu Yasir narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women and perfume have been made beloved to me, and the coolness of my eye has been placed in prayer."
"3484","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Marhum ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: He said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a daughter of his was with him. Anas said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and offered herself to him. His daughter said: How little her shyness is! He said: She is better than you; she offered herself to the Prophet."
"3485","Abdullah ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father Abd al-Samad ibn Ali narrated to us, from Awwam al-Basri, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The day of Friday and the night of Friday are twenty-four hours; there is no hour in them except that Allah has therein six hundred freed from the Fire. He said: Then we left him and entered upon al-Hasan, and we mentioned to him the hadith of Thabit, and he said: I heard it, and he added in it: all of them having deserved the Fire."
"3486","Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his supplication: O Allah, turn my heart toward Your religion, and protect those behind us by Your mercy."
"3487","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) migrated, he was riding with Abu Bakr behind him. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq knew the road from his differing journeys to Syria. They would pass by people who would say: Who is this with you? He would say: A guide guiding me. When they drew near Medina, they sent to the people who had embraced Islam among the Ansar, to Abu Umama and his companions, and they came out to meet them. They said: Enter safe and obeyed. So they entered. Anas said: I never saw a day brighter or more beautiful than the day on which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr entered Medina."
"3488","Amr ibn Husayn narrated to us, Hassan ibn Siyah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he performed ablution, would run his fingers through his beard."
"3489","Amr ibn Husayn narrated to us, Ali ibn Abi Sarah narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing has worn away Islam like miserliness."
"3490","Ahmad ibn al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Atiyya al-Ayshi narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come out to the mosque in which were the Muhajirun and the Ansar; none of them would raise his head from his huddled sitting posture except Abu Bakr and Umar, for he would smile at them and they would smile at him."
"3491","Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min narrated to us, Ali ibn Abi Sarah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of Paradise will look down upon the people of the Fire, and a man of the Fire will call to him: O so-and-so, do you not know me? He will say: No, by Allah, I do not know you; who are you, woe to you? He will say: I am the one whom you passed by in the world and you asked me for a drink of water and I gave you to drink, so intercede for me for it with your Lord. He said: That man will enter upon Allah in His courtyard and say: O my Lord, I looked down upon the people of the Fire, and a man of the Fire stood and called: O so-and-so, do you not know me? I said: No, by Allah, I do not know you, and who are you? He said: I am the one whom you passed by in the world and you asked me to drink and I gave you to drink, so intercede for me for it with your Lord. O my Lord, so allow me to intercede for him. He said: So Allah will allow him to intercede for him and will bring him out of the Fire."
"3492","Abdullah, the brother of al-Muqaddami, narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us: He said: Whenever I came to Anas, he would be informed of my whereabouts and I would enter upon him; I would take his two hands and kiss them, saying: May my father be ransom for these two hands that touched the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And I would kiss his two eyes, saying: May my father be ransom for these two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3493","Al-Muqaddami Abdullah narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, from Thabit: He said: Whenever I came to Anas, he would call for perfume and wipe his hands and his cheeks with it."
"3494","Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to me, my father narrated to us, from Jamila, the mother of the child of Anas ibn Malik: She said: When Thabit came to Anas, Anas would say: O slave girl, bring me perfume so I may wipe my hands, for the son of the mother of Thabit, when he comes, is not satisfied until he kisses my hands."
"3495","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ijli narrated to us, Ali ibn Abi Sarah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: A man with white head and beard entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Are you not a Muslim? He said: Yes, indeed. He said: Then dye (your hair)."
"3496","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Abu Qutayba Salm ibn Qutayba al-Shairi narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to us this verse: Indeed, those who said, Our Lord is Allah, then remained steadfast. And he said: People have said it, then most of them disbelieved; so whoever says it until he dies is among those who remained steadfast upon it."
"3497","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of you? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The best of you are those with the longest lives, when they remain upright."
"3498","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man of Paradise will be brought and it will be said: O son of Adam, how did you find your abode? He will say: O my Lord, the best abode. It will be said to him: Ask and wish. He will say: I ask and wish for nothing except that You return me to the world and I be killed ten times, for what he sees of the virtue of martyrdom. And a man of the Fire will be brought and it will be said: O son of Adam, how did you find your abode? He will say: O my Lord, the worst abode. Would you ransom yourself with the earth full of gold? He will say: Yes, O my Lord. He will say: You have lied; I asked you for what was easier than this, and he will be returned to the Fire."
"3499","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no soul that dies having good with Allah that wishes to return to the world, except the martyr, for he wishes to return to the world and be killed, for what he sees of the virtue of martyrdom."
"3500","Hudba narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Buraq, a white animal above the donkey and below the mule, placing its hoof where its glance ends. He said: I rode it until it went with me to Bayt al-Maqdis. I tied the animal to the ring to which the prophets tie. Then I entered the mosque and prayed in it two rakahs. Then I came out, and Jibril brought me a vessel of wine and a vessel of milk; I took the milk, and Jibril said to me: You have chosen the fitrah. He said: Then he took us up to the lowest heaven. Jibril sought entry; it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. It was opened for us, and I met Adam, and he welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then he took us up to the second heaven. Jibril sought entry; it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. It was opened for us, and I met the two sons of the maternal aunt, Yahya and Isa, and they welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then he took us up to the third heaven. Jibril sought entry; it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. It was opened for us, and I met Yusuf, and he had been given half of beauty; he welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then we were taken up to the fourth heaven. Jibril sought entry; it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. It was opened for us, and I met Idris; he welcomed me and supplicated good for me. He said: Allah says: And We raised him to a high station. Then he took us up to the fifth heaven. Jibril sought entry; it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. It was opened for us, and there was Harun; he welcomed me and supplicated good for me. Then he took us up to the sixth heaven. Jibril sought entry; it was said: Who are you? He said: Jibril. It was said: Who is with you? He said: Muhammad. It was said: Has he been sent for? He said: He has been sent for. It was opened for us, and I met Ibrahim, leaning his back against the House, into which seventy thousand angels enter every day and then never return to it. Then he took me to Sidrat al-Muntaha; its leaves were like elephant ears and its fruits like large jars. When it was covered by what covered it of the command of Allah, it changed, and no one of Allah's creation can describe it well for its beauty. He said: Then there was revealed to me what was revealed, and fifty prayers were made obligatory upon me every day. He said: I descended to Musa, and he said: What was made obligatory upon your ummah? He said: I said: Fifty prayers every day and night. He said: Your ummah cannot bear that; return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction. He said: I returned to my Lord and said: O my Lord, lighten for my ummah. He reduced five from me. I returned to Musa and he said: What did you do? He said: I said: He reduced five from me. He said: Your ummah cannot bear that; return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction. I continued returning to my Lord asking for reduction, between my Lord and Musa, until He said: O Muhammad, they are five prayers every day and night; each prayer counts as ten, so that is fifty prayers. Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, one good deed is written; if he does it, ten are written. Whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, nothing is upon him; if he does it, one evil deed is written. I returned to Musa and informed him. He said: Return to your Lord and ask Him for reduction. He said: I have returned to my Lord until I felt shy."
"3501","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Thabit, from Anas: Haritha went out to look around, and an arrow struck him and killed him. His mother said: O Messenger of Allah, you know the place of Haritha with me; if he is in Paradise I will be patient, otherwise you will see what I do. He said: O mother of Haritha, it is not one Paradise, but many Paradises, and Haritha is in the best of them. Or he said: In the highest of al-Firdaws. Yazid said: I am in doubt."
"3502","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) practiced continuous fasting at the end of the month, and people practiced it. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If the month were extended for us, I would continue fasting continuously, so that those who go to extremes would abandon their extremism. You are not like me; I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"3503","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"3504","Zuhayr narrated to us, Habban narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Humayd and Thabit, from Anas: He said: I gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to drink in this cup: water, milk, nabidh, and honey."
"3505","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us: He said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying to a woman of his family: Do you know so-and-so? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by her while she was weeping over a grave. He said to her: Fear Allah and be patient. She said to him: Go away from me, for you do not care about my calamity. He said: She had not recognized him. It was said to her: This is the Messenger of Allah. She was seized as if by death. She came to his door and found no gatekeeper at it. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not recognize you. He said: Patience is at the first shock."
"3506","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard a rustling; I said: What is this rustling? It was said: Al-Rumaysa, the daughter of Milhan."
"3507","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw sputum in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it off with his hand."
"3508","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached by Jibril while he was playing with the boys. He took him, threw him down, and split open his heart. He extracted a clot from it and said: This is the share of Satan from you. Then he washed it in a basin of gold with Zamzam water, then joined it together and returned it to its place. The boys came running to his mother, meaning his foster mother, saying: Muhammad has been killed. She received him while his color had changed. Anas said: I used to see the trace of the stitching on his chest. And sometimes Hammad said: An angel came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3509","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Qatada, Humayd, and Thabit informed us, from Anas: Some people of Urayna came to Medina and found its climate unsuitable. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them to the camels of charity, saying: Drink their urine and their milk. They killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), drove off the camels, and apostatized from Islam. They were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he cut off their hands and feet on opposite sides, gouged their eyes, and cast them in al-Harra. Anas said: I used to see one of them biting the earth with his mouth until they died. And sometimes Hammad said: gnawing the earth with his mouth until they died."
"3510","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: The people said: O Messenger of Allah, wealth has perished; we are suffering drought, O Messenger of Allah, and wealth has perished, so pray for rain for us. He stood on Friday while on the pulpit and prayed for rain; Hammad described the spreading of his hands opposite his chest, with the palms of his hands toward the ground. There was not a wisp of cloud in the sky. He did not leave until the strong young man was concerned about himself returning to his family. He said: We were rained upon until the next Friday. They said: O Messenger of Allah, buildings have collapsed and travelers have been cut off, so supplicate Allah to remove it from us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. He said: It cleared away until Medina was as if in a crown."
"3511","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: Umm Sulaym was with Abu Talha on the day of Hunayn, and Umm Sulaym had a dagger with her. Abu Talha said: What is this with you, O Umm Sulaym? She said: I took it so that if any of the disbelievers comes near me I will rip open his belly with it. Abu Talha said: O Prophet of Allah, do you not hear what Umm Sulaym says, she says such-and-such. She said: O Messenger of Allah, kill those after us among the freed captives, they fled from you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Umm Sulaym, indeed Allah has sufficed and done good."
"3512","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man among his Companions who was sick and had become like a chick. He said to him: Did you ask Allah for anything? He said: I said: O Allah, whatever You would punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You have no strength for the punishment of Allah; why did you not say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"3513","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man of the Ansar and said: O maternal uncle, say: there is no god but Allah. He said: Maternal uncle or paternal uncle? He said: No, rather maternal uncle. And he said: Is it better for me to say it? He said: Yes."
"3514","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas, who said: I gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to drink with this cup of mine all kinds of drink: honey, nabidh, and milk."
"3515","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten the rows, straighten the rows, for by Allah I see you from behind me as I see you from before me."
"3516","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas: when the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they said: Send with us a man to teach us the Sunna and Islam. So he took the hand of Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah and said: This is the trustworthy one of this nation."
"3517","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: a man said: O Messenger of Allah, where is my father? He said: In the Fire. When he turned away he called him and said: My father and your father are in the Fire."
"3518","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was once met by the children of the Ansar and the slave girls, and he said: By Allah, I love you."
"3519","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas: a woman who had something wrong with her mind said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need. He said: O mother of so-and-so, choose whichever road you wish. So he stood with her conversing privately until she fulfilled her need."
"3520","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas: the sister of al-Rubayyi ibn Haritha wounded a person, so they disputed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: O Messenger of Allah, retaliation, retaliation. The mother of al-Rubayyi said: O Messenger of Allah, will retaliation be taken from so-and-so? No, by Allah, it will not be taken from her. She kept insisting until they accepted the blood money. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the servants of Allah there are those who, if they swear by Allah, Allah fulfills it."
"3521","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he will be known."
"3522","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most severely afflicted person in this world among the people of Paradise will be brought, and Allah will say: Dip him in Paradise once. So he will be dipped in it once, and Allah will say: O son of Adam, did you ever see misery, or anything you dislike? He will say: No, by Your might, I never saw anything I dislike. Then the most pampered person in this world among the people of the Fire will be brought, and Allah will say: Dip him once in the Fire. So he will be dipped in it. He will say: O son of Adam, did you ever see any good, any joy of the eye? He will say: No, by Your might, I never saw any good nor any joy of the eye."
"3523","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Qatada, Thabit, and Humayd narrated to us, from Anas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to open the prayer with: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And Humayd did not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3524","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, who said: when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to his bed, he said: Praise be to Allah who fed us, gave us drink, sufficed us, and sheltered us; and how many are those who have no sufficer and no shelter."
"3525","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas reporting from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There will remain of Paradise what Allah wills to remain, then Allah will originate for it a creation of whatever He wills."
"3526","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to often say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"3527","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until Allah, Allah is no longer said on the earth."
"3528","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: We used to say that the Hour will not come until the sky does not rain, the earth does not grow, until one caretaker is left for fifty women, and until a woman passes by a man and he seizes her and looks at her and says: This woman once had a husband. Hammad mentioned it thus, and Hammad also mentioned it from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), without doubt. And he also said: from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as I recall."
"3529","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw as if I were in the house of Uqba ibn Rafi, and we were brought fresh dates of Ibn Tab. So I interpreted it as elevation for us in this world, a good end in the Hereafter, and that our religion has become good."
"3530","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit informed us, from Anas: he recited this verse: Indeed We have given you al-Kawthar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given al-Kawthar, and behold a river flowing without being dug; its banks are domes of pearl. I struck my hand to its soil and it was fragrant musk, and its pebbles were pearls."
"3531","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Made beloved to me of this world are women and perfume, and the coolness of my eye was placed in prayer."
"3532","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Thabit from Anas: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard sounds and said: What are these sounds? They said: The palm trees, they are pollinating them, O Messenger of Allah. He said: If they did not do it, it would still be fine. So they did not pollinate that year, and it became poor unripe dates. They mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: If a matter is of your worldly affairs, it is up to you; and if a matter is of your religion, then refer it to me."
"3533","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he saw an old man being supported between his two sons and said: What is the matter with him? They said: O Messenger of Allah, he vowed to walk. He said: Allah is free of need of this man tormenting himself. Then he ordered him, so he rode."
"3534","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas: the Jews, when a woman menstruated, would not eat with her nor stay with her in the houses. So the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah revealed: They ask you about menstruation; say: It is harm, so keep away from women during menstruation, to the end of the verse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do everything except intercourse. That reached the Jews, and they said: This man does not want to leave anything of our affair but he opposes us in it. Then Usayd ibn Hudayr and Abbad ibn Bishr came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews said such-and-such; shall we not stay together with them? The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed color until we thought he was angry with them. They left, and a gift of milk met them; so he sent after them and gave them to drink, and we knew he was not angry with them."
"3535","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he supplicated, would make the outer sides of his palms face his face."
"3536","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Hammad informed us, from Thabit, from Anas: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until it was said: He has fasted; and he would break his fast until it was said: He has broken his fast."
"3537","Abu Khaythama Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a silver ring on his right hand with an Abyssinian stone, and he would turn its stone to the inside of his palm."
"3538","Yahya ibn Ayyub and Ibn Qudama narrated to us, both saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli informed us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, saying: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a ring of silver, and its stone was Abyssinian."
"3539","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: he saw a ring of silver on the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So the people made rings of silver; then he threw away his ring, and the people threw away their rings."
"3540","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the Conquest wearing a helmet on his head. It was said: This is Ibn Khatal, clinging to the curtains of the Kaba. He said: Kill him."
"3541","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah wearing a helmet."
"3542","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in the year of the Conquest wearing a helmet. It was said: This is Ibn Khatal, clinging to the curtains of the Kaba. He said: Kill him."
"3543","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah wearing a helmet."
"3544","Hadbaha narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, and I know it only from Anas: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the privy, would remove his ring."
"3545","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver with an Abyssinian stone, and its engraving was: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"3546","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba and the muzaffat to make nabidh in."
"3547","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, raising it: When dinner is present and the prayer is established, begin with dinner."
"3548","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, similar to it."
"3549","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The last look I cast at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on Monday. He lifted the curtain while the people were behind Abu Bakr. I looked at his face as if it were a page of a mushaf. The people wanted to move, so he gestured to them to stay. He let down the curtain, and he died at the end of that day."
"3550","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who heard it from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, do not sever ties, and be servants of Allah as brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."
"3551","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I memorized these four from al-Zuhri, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sever ties, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers; and it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."
"3552","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"3553","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madina when I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty. My mothers would urge me to serve him. He entered our house, and we milked for him from a domestic sheep, mixed for him with water from a well in the house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, and Umar said to him - while Abu Bakr was on his left -: O Messenger of Allah, give Abu Bakr. So he gave it to a Bedouin on his right, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"3554","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who heard it from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, similar to it."
"3555","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I memorized from al-Zuhri, repeatedly, that he heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madina when I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty years old, and my mothers would urge me to serve him."
"3556","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I memorized from al-Zuhri, repeatedly, that he heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered our house, and we milked for him from a domestic sheep, and it was mixed for him with water from a well in the house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, with Abu Bakr on his left and a Bedouin on his right, and Umar aside. Umar said: Give Abu Bakr. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed it to the Bedouin and said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"3557","Abu Khaythama and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: And what have you prepared for it? He said: He did not mention good, but: I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with whom you love."
"3558","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Hour, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared much deed for it, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: A person is with whom he loves."
"3559","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba and Abu Khaythama narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a horse and his right side was scraped. The prayer came and he led us in prayer sitting. When he finished his prayer, he said: The imam was made only to be followed; when he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he rises, rise; when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You is praise; and when he prays sitting, pray sitting all together."
"3560","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a wedding feast for Safiyya. I think he said: With dates and sawiq."
"3561","Ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank standing."
"3562","And he narrated it to us another time: Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank standing, with a Bedouin on his right and Abu Bakr on his left. So he gave it to the Bedouin and said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"3563","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought milk and drank. He said: Abu Bakr was on his left and a Bedouin on his right. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, hand it to Abu Bakr. He said: So he handed it to the Bedouin."
"3564","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say the talbiya: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise, blessing, and dominion are Yours; there is no partner for You."
"3565","Wahb ibn Baqiyya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking, with Abu Bakr on his left and a Bedouin man on his right. So he gave the Bedouin his remainder, then said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"3566","Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: He saw a silver ring on the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, so he made rings of silver and they wore them. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw away his ring, and the people threw away their rings. And he saw a gold ring on a man's hand, so he struck his finger a blow. And he saw two gold earrings on Umm Salama, so he turned away from her until she threw it away."
"3567","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, Abu Ali ibn Yazid informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: And We ordained for them therein: a life for a life and an eye for an eye."
"3568","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil and others narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak; Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill with the illness in which he died, Bilal came to him and called the adhan for prayer. He said: O Bilal, you have conveyed; whoever wishes, let him pray, and whoever wishes, let him leave it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then who will lead the people in prayer? He said: Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. When Abu Bakr stepped forward, the curtains were lifted from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we looked at him as if he were a white page, wearing a black cloak. Abu Bakr thought he wanted to come out, so he stepped back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to pray in your place. So Abu Bakr prayed, and we did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he died that day."
"3569","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Usama ibn Zayd, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Hamza - his nose cut off and he mutilated - and said: Were it not that Safiyya would grieve, I would have left him until Allah gathers him from the bellies of beasts and birds. So he was shrouded in a striped cloak; when his head was covered, his feet showed, and when his feet were covered, his head showed. So they covered his head. And he did not pray over any of the martyrs, and he said: I am a witness over you today. And he would gather three in one grave, and two in one grave, and ask: Which of them knew most Quran? Then he would advance him in the lahd. And he would shroud two men and three in a single garment."
"3570","Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would gesture during prayer."
"3571","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq al-Madani narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked Allah for the heedless ones among the progeny of mankind, and He gave them to me."
"3572","Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered during the Umra of the Fulfillment with Ibn Rawaha before him, saying:"
"3573","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Qurra ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, that Ibn Shihab narrated to him from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became a prophet when he was forty years old. He stayed in Makkah ten years and in Madina ten years, and he died at sixty years old, and there were not twenty white hairs in his head and beard."
"3574","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Muawiya ibn Yahya al-Sadafi, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every religion has a character, and the character of this religion is modesty."
"3575","Salih ibn Malik Abu Abdullah narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every nation has a trustworthy one, and this is ours; and he took the hand of Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah."
"3576","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The one among them most resembling the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was al-Hasan ibn Ali."
"3577","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Usama narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar; Usama said: And al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Uhud, he heard the women of the Ansar weeping. He said: But Hamza has no mourners. That reached the women of the Ansar, so they wept for Hamza. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept, then woke while they were weeping. He said: Woe to them, they have continued weeping since today; let them weep, but let them not weep over one who perishes after today."
"3578","Wahb ibn Baqiyya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When dinner is present and the prayer is established, begin with it, and do not rush away from your dinner."
"3579","Zuhayr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Yunus narrating from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, place in Madina double the blessing that is in Makkah."
"3580","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, Anas ibn Malik informed me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah during the Umra of the Fulfillment with Ibn Rawaha holding his stirrup, saying:"
"3581","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, Wail ibn Dawud narrated to us, from his son Bakr ibn Wail, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a wedding feast for Safiyya with sawiq and dates. Sufyan said: I heard it from al-Zuhri narrating it, but I did not memorize it; and Bakr ibn Wail used to sit with al-Zuhri along with us."
"3582","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, Anas ibn Malik informed me: He heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying while in Madina: O Allah, place in it double the blessing that is in Makkah."
"3583","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized Asad ibn Zurara for a thorn."
"3584","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madina while it was feverish, and the people got fever. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque while the people were sitting praying. He said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing. He said: So the people exerted themselves to pray standing."
"3585","Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Talha ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a silver ring on his right hand with an Abyssinian stone, and its stone was toward his palm."
"3586","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Samina al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Al-Hasan ibn Ali was the one among them most resembling in face the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3587","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Samina narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: I saw on Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a striped silk shirt."
"3588","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abu Damra narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Hawd is between Ayla and Sana of Yemen, and in it are pitchers numbering the stars of the sky."
"3589","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would gesture during prayer."
"3590","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding what is prepared in vessels and the muzaffata and the dubba, and he said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"3591","Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Ghadidi Abu Jafar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Qurra ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He became a prophet when he was forty; he stayed in Makkah ten years and in Madina ten years; and he died when he was sixty, and there were not twenty white hairs in his head and beard."
"3592","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, Anas ibn Malik narrated to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would love to have two valleys; nothing will fill his mouth but dust; and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"3593","Abu Musa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib and Uqayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man selling the stud fee of his horse."
"3594","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, that he informed him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Asr while the sun was high and alive; then one going would go to al-Awali while the sun was still high."
"3595","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, the nephew of al-Zuhri narrated to us, from his uncle, who said: Anas ibn Malik informed me: Some people of the Ansar said on the day of Hunayn, when Allah granted His Messenger the wealth of Hawazin as spoils, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began giving men of Quraysh a hundred camels each. They said: May Allah forgive the Messenger of Allah; he gives Quraysh and leaves us while our swords drip with their blood? Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of their saying, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to the Ansar and gathered them in a tent of leather, calling no one else with them. When they gathered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them and said: What is this report that reached me about you? The men of understanding among the Ansar said to him: As for our men of judgment, O Messenger of Allah, they said nothing; but some of us, young in age, said: May Allah forgive the Messenger of Allah; does he give Quraysh and leave us while our swords drip with their blood? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I give those newly accustomed to disbelief, to reconcile them. Are you not pleased that the people go with wealth while you return to your homes with the Messenger of Allah? By Allah, what you return with is better than what they return with. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we are pleased. He said to them: You will find after me severe preference, so be patient until you meet Allah and His Messenger, for I am at the Hawd. Anas said: They said: Yes."
"3596","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, having heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a horse and his right side was scraped. We visited him, then the prayer came and he led us in prayer sitting, and we prayed behind him sitting. When he finished the prayer, he said: The imam was made only to be followed; when he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he prostrates, prostrate; when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You is praise; and when he prays sitting, pray sitting all together. Abu Yaqub said: Sufyan narrated it to us another time, saying: Our Lord, and to You is praise."
"3597","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The last look I cast at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he lifted the curtain on the day he died, and I looked at his face as if it were a page of a mushaf. Then he gestured to the people to stay - and he let down the curtain, and he died at the end of that day - while they were in rows behind Abu Bakr."
"3598","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, having heard Anas saying: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Hour and said: What have you prepared for it? He said - as if he did not mention much -: Except that I love Allah and His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then you are with whom you love."
"3599","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When dinner is present and the prayer is established, begin with dinner."
"3600","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the dubba and the muzaffat to make nabidh in."
